   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/problem-solvers-caucus-endorses-dignity-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Problem Solvers Caucus Endorses the Dignity Act | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Senator (D-DE), Cleaning Coalition of America, Essential Worker Immigration Coalition, Ethics & Religious Liberty Commission of the Southern Baptist Convention, Florida Farm Bureau Federation, Florida Fruit & Vegetable Association, Florida Tomato Exchange, FWD.us , Hispanic Leadership Fund, Ideaspace, Immigration Hub, Improve the Dream, Invest in the USA (IIUSA), Ken Salazar, U.S."
  },
  {
   "id": 101,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/problem-solvers-caucus-endorses-dignity-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Problem Solvers Caucus Endorses the Dignity Act | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Ambassador to Mexico, LIBRE Initiative, Mason Contractors Association of America, National Association of Counties, National Association of Evangelicals, NAFSA: Association of International Educators, National Association of Landscape Professionals, National Immigration Forum, National Latino Evangelical Coalition, National Retail Federation (NRF), Niskanen Center, Outdoor Amusement Business Association (OABA), Power & Communication Contractors Association, Presidents’ Alliance on Higher Education and Immigration, Public Affairs Alliance of Iranian Americans, Puerto Rican Chamber of Commerce of Central Florida, TechNet, TESOL International Association, Texas Border Coalition, Texas Impact, The Legal Immigration and Border Enforcement Reform this Year (LIBERTY) Campaign, UnidosUS, U."
  },
  {
   "id": 102,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/problem-solvers-caucus-endorses-dignity-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Problem Solvers Caucus Endorses the Dignity Act | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "S. Chamber of Commerce, U.S. Conference of Catholic Bishops (USCCB), U.S. Hispanic Business Council, U.S. Travel Association, and World Relief. Securing the Border and Restoring Law and Order Provides $25 billion to fully secure the border. Mandates 100% nationwide E-verify to ensure all American businesses are hiring legal workers. Achieves operational control and advantage of the Southern Border by employing a comprehensive Southern Border Strategy. Constructs enhanced physical barriers and deploys the most up-to-date technology at the border. Hires thousands of new Border Patrol agents, CBP officers, and border intelligence units."
  },
  {
   "id": 103,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/problem-solvers-caucus-endorses-dignity-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Problem Solvers Caucus Endorses the Dignity Act | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Implements new policies to stop criminals crossing the border illegally, including new authorities to track cartel spotters, and raises penalties on human traffickers and child sex traffickers. Authorizes DHS to officially designate an organization as a criminal street gang, making any alien involved in a criminal gang inadmissible and deportable. Designates Mexican cartels as Special Transnational Criminal Organizations. Directs DHS to complete and implement biometric exit at all air, land, and sea ports-of-entry for international travelers. Provides DHS the authority to use DNA testing to verify family relationships."
  },
  {
   "id": 104,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/problem-solvers-caucus-endorses-dignity-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Problem Solvers Caucus Endorses the Dignity Act | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Enhances port-of-entry security by expanding surveillance and intrusion detection systems. Improves legal commerce and trade by expanding inspection lanes and investing in X-ray technology to safely inspect commercial vehicles. Expedites processing and ends catch-and-release policies. Establishes at least five Humanitarian Campuses (HC) that will receive individuals and families arriving at the southern border for immediate processing. Asylum-seekers will remain at an HC until their case is decided. They will have freedom of movement within the HC, access to state-of-the-art facilities, medical personal, legal counsel, and non-governmental organizations."
  },
  {
   "id": 105,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/problem-solvers-caucus-endorses-dignity-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Problem Solvers Caucus Endorses the Dignity Act | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Decides asylum cases within 60 days. Asylum-seekers will undergo an initial credible fear interview within 15 days of their arrival and further screening by trained asylum officers for final determination within an additional 45 days. *Complex cases may be referred to case management to await a hearing before an Immigration Judge. Creates five additional immigration centers in Latin America to stop migrant caravans and prevent individuals from making the dangerous land journey to the United States. The centers will offer asylum pre-screening, child reunification services, and employment counsel to determine eligibility for work visas in the United States."
  },
  {
   "id": 106,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/problem-solvers-caucus-endorses-dignity-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Problem Solvers Caucus Endorses the Dignity Act | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Implements a security and development strategy to address instability in Central America. This will help bring stability and economic development to Guatemala, El Salvador, and Honduras. Increases U.S. authorities to target transnational criminals, smugglers, human traffickers, drug traffickers, and gangs like MS-13. Cracks down on asylum fraud by increasing penalties for those that make false statements or provide false documentation. Establishes a new two-strike policy for anyone caught crossing at a non-port-of-entry, to ensure legitimate asylum seekers are processed appropriately while bad actors are apprehended. Giving Dignity and Redemption to Undocumented Immigrants"
  },
  {
   "id": 107,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/problem-solvers-caucus-endorses-dignity-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Problem Solvers Caucus Endorses the Dignity Act | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Creates immediate protected status and streamlined path for Dreamers and TPS recipients, as outlined in the Dream and Promise Act. Establishes the Dignity Program, a practical solution for undocumented immigrants who have been in the U.S. for more than five years. Recipients will be offered a chance to work, pay restitution, get right with the law, and earn legal status. Applicants must comply with all federal and state laws, pass a criminal background check, and pay outstanding taxes or debts. Dignity participants will also pay $5,000 in restitution during the seven years of the program, check in with DHS every two years, and remain in good public standing."
  },
  {
   "id": 108,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/problem-solvers-caucus-endorses-dignity-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Problem Solvers Caucus Endorses the Dignity Act | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Individuals in the Dignity Program will not have access to federal means-tested benefits or entitlements. Establishes two options after successful completion of the Dignity Program – Dignity Status or the Redemption Program: Dignity Status: Dignity recipients who choose this option will immediately receive a five-year Dignity Status, which provides full work authorization, the ability to live in the U.S., and travel authorization outside the U.S. They will also remain ineligible for citizenship, means-tested benefits, and entitlements. Dignity Status can be renewed an indefinite number of times as long as the individual remains in good standing with the law."
  },
  {
   "id": 109,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/salazar-wasserman-schultz-reintroduce-bipartisan-bill-make-condos-safer-and",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "SALAZAR, WASSERMAN SCHULTZ REINTRODUCE BIPARTISAN BILL TO MAKE CONDOS SAFER AND MORE AFFORDABLE | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "SALAZAR, WASSERMAN SCHULTZ REINTRODUCE BIPARTISAN BILL TO MAKE CONDOS SAFER AND MORE AFFORDABLE | Representative Maria Salazar SALAZAR, WASSERMAN SCHULTZ REINTRODUCE BIPARTISAN BILL TO MAKE CONDOS SAFER AND MORE AFFORDABLE Washington, DC – This week, U.S. Representatives María Elvira Salazar (FL-27) and Debbie Wasserman Schultz (FL-25) reintroduced the bipartisan Making Condos Safer and Affordable Act to help condominium owners afford critical structural and safety repairs. The legislation gives families greater access to financing for required building improvements, helping them stay in their homes while keeping their communities safe."
  },
  {
   "id": 110,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/salazar-wasserman-schultz-reintroduce-bipartisan-bill-make-condos-safer-and",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "SALAZAR, WASSERMAN SCHULTZ REINTRODUCE BIPARTISAN BILL TO MAKE CONDOS SAFER AND MORE AFFORDABLE | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "The bill expands access to two loan programs guaranteed by the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD), allowing condominium owners to finance special assessments required by their homeowners' or condominium associations for structural integrity and life-safety repairs. It also supports compliance with the updated building safety requirements enacted after the tragic Surfside condominium collapse that claimed 98 lives."
  },
  {
   "id": 111,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/salazar-wasserman-schultz-reintroduce-bipartisan-bill-make-condos-safer-and",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "SALAZAR, WASSERMAN SCHULTZ REINTRODUCE BIPARTISAN BILL TO MAKE CONDOS SAFER AND MORE AFFORDABLE | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "“The Surfside tragedy changed our community forever and reminded us that protecting families must always come first. As we honor those we lost, we must take action to help prevent another disaster,” said Salazar . “This bipartisan bill gives condominium associations and homeowners the tools they need to finance critical safety repairs, protect residents, and preserve safe, affordable housing across South Florida.”"
  },
  {
   "id": 112,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/salazar-wasserman-schultz-reintroduce-bipartisan-bill-make-condos-safer-and",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "SALAZAR, WASSERMAN SCHULTZ REINTRODUCE BIPARTISAN BILL TO MAKE CONDOS SAFER AND MORE AFFORDABLE | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "“Five years ago, an unimaginable but entirely preventable tragedy rocked our South Florida community with the collapse of Surfside's Champlain Towers, claiming 98 innocent lives. While the cause was finally identified after years of investigations, action is still needed to stop this from happening again,” said Wasserman Schultz. “My bipartisan Making Condos Safer and Affordable Act ensures condominium associations can afford to make pressing repairs and keep residents safe.” Key Provisions of the Making Condos Safer and Affordable Act:"
  },
  {
   "id": 113,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/salazar-wasserman-schultz-reintroduce-bipartisan-bill-make-condos-safer-and",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "SALAZAR, WASSERMAN SCHULTZ REINTRODUCE BIPARTISAN BILL TO MAKE CONDOS SAFER AND MORE AFFORDABLE | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Expands the FHA 203(k) loan program to allow condominium owners to use these loans to help cover special assessments for critical structural and safety repairs. Strengthens the Title I Property Improvement Loan program by expanding federal loan insurance for private lenders financing special assessments for individual condominium owners and condominium associations. The bill also raises the maximum insured loan amount to $55,000, with future adjustments for inflation. Simplifies the loan application process to make it easier for condominium owners and associations to access financing for necessary repairs."
  },
  {
   "id": 114,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/salazar-wasserman-schultz-reintroduce-bipartisan-bill-make-condos-safer-and",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "SALAZAR, WASSERMAN SCHULTZ REINTRODUCE BIPARTISAN BILL TO MAKE CONDOS SAFER AND MORE AFFORDABLE | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Authorizes the Federal Housing Administration (FHA) to insure condominium association rehabilitation loans under Section 234 of the National Housing Act. Provides condominium associations with greater financing flexibility by allowing FHA-insured rehabilitation loans to be secured by future assessment income, real property, or a combination of both. Expands the eligible use of FHA-insured association loans to include the rehabilitation, repair, alteration, improvement, or replacement of a condominium project's common systems, infrastructure, and shared facilities."
  },
  {
   "id": 115,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/salazar-wasserman-schultz-reintroduce-bipartisan-bill-make-condos-safer-and",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "SALAZAR, WASSERMAN SCHULTZ REINTRODUCE BIPARTISAN BILL TO MAKE CONDOS SAFER AND MORE AFFORDABLE | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Protects taxpayers by limiting FHA insurance to 90 percent of rehabilitation costs, consistent with existing FHA multifamily rehabilitation insurance programs. This legislation is endorsed by the Community Associations Institute. As a member of the House Financial Services Committee, Rep. Salazar has advanced bipartisan legislation to expand housing opportunities, strengthen homeownership, improve affordability, and deliver practical solutions to the housing challenges facing South Florida and communities across the country."
  },
  {
   "id": 116,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/salazar-wasserman-schultz-reintroduce-bipartisan-bill-make-condos-safer-and",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "SALAZAR, WASSERMAN SCHULTZ REINTRODUCE BIPARTISAN BILL TO MAKE CONDOS SAFER AND MORE AFFORDABLE | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "The RESIDE Act , legislation introduced by Rep. Salazar to help communities convert vacant and underutilized properties into attainable housing. The bill was incorporated into the final bipartisan 21st Century ROAD to Housing Act , which passed both the House and Senate and is awaiting the President's signature. Securing $3.5 million in federal funding for the Flagler Affordable Senior Housing Project in the City of Miami, helping expand affordable housing opportunities for low-income seniors in South Florida."
  },
  {
   "id": 117,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/salazar-wasserman-schultz-reintroduce-bipartisan-bill-make-condos-safer-and",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "SALAZAR, WASSERMAN SCHULTZ REINTRODUCE BIPARTISAN BILL TO MAKE CONDOS SAFER AND MORE AFFORDABLE | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "The Home Advantage for American Families Act , legislation to help keep the American Dream of homeownership within reach by limiting the impact of large institutional and foreign investors that drive up housing costs for American families. The Shelter Act , bipartisan legislation that provides targeted tax incentives to help homeowners and small businesses strengthen their properties against future natural disasters."
  },
  {
   "id": 118,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/salazar-wasserman-schultz-reintroduce-bipartisan-bill-make-condos-safer-and",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "SALAZAR, WASSERMAN SCHULTZ REINTRODUCE BIPARTISAN BILL TO MAKE CONDOS SAFER AND MORE AFFORDABLE | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "The Making Condos Safer and Affordable Act builds on Rep. Salazar's work to preserve homeownership by giving condominium owners and associations the financial tools they need to finance critical structural and safety repairs, comply with updated building safety requirements, and help keep Florida families safely in their homes."
  },
  {
   "id": 119,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/salazar-delivers-35-million-federal-funding-affordable-housing-senior-citizens",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Salazar Delivers $3.5 Million in Federal Funding for Affordable Housing for Senior Citizens in Miami | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Salazar Delivers $3.5 Million in Federal Funding for Affordable Housing for Senior Citizens in Miami | Representative Maria Salazar Salazar Delivers $3.5 Million in Federal Funding for Affordable Housing for Senior Citizens in Miami MIAMI, FL – Today, Rep. María Elvira Salazar (R-FL) joined the Miami City Commission to unveil a $3.5 million investment in new affordable housing in the City for senior citizens."
  },
  {
   "id": 120,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/salazar-delivers-35-million-federal-funding-affordable-housing-senior-citizens",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Salazar Delivers $3.5 Million in Federal Funding for Affordable Housing for Senior Citizens in Miami | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "The funding will go towards the construction of the Flagler Affordable Senior Housing Project, a Community Funding Project requested and approved in the Fiscal Year 2024 Consolidated Appropriations Act, legislation the Congresswoman proudly supported . This project will add a significant number of new housing units for seniors in our community."
  },
  {
   "id": 121,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/salazar-delivers-35-million-federal-funding-affordable-housing-senior-citizens",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Salazar Delivers $3.5 Million in Federal Funding for Affordable Housing for Senior Citizens in Miami | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "“ Today, I want to present this check for $3.5 million for our seniors in Miami, ” said Rep. Salazar. “ This funding will go towards the Flagler Affordable Senior Housing Project – giving safe, beautiful, and affordable living to seniors in our community. That is the way we treat those who paid and gave our community years of labor and contributions to the Social Security system. ” The new affordable housing project for senior citizens is one of many of Rep. Salazar’s initiatives to address the affordability and safe housing crisis facing South Florida. Other legislation and projects the Congresswoman has championed or supported include:"
  },
  {
   "id": 122,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/salazar-delivers-35-million-federal-funding-affordable-housing-senior-citizens",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Salazar Delivers $3.5 Million in Federal Funding for Affordable Housing for Senior Citizens in Miami | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Introduced H.R. 3533 , the Home Advantage for American Families Act. This legislation increases the real estate sales tax for foreign buyers, ensuring Americans are not priced out of the market. Introduced H.R. 4305 , the Shelter Act. This legislation provides a tax credit to working families and small businesses to invest in disaster mitigation improvements to make their homes and property more resilient."
  },
  {
   "id": 123,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/salazar-delivers-35-million-federal-funding-affordable-housing-senior-citizens",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Salazar Delivers $3.5 Million in Federal Funding for Affordable Housing for Senior Citizens in Miami | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Supported H.R. 7024 , the Tax Relief for American Families and Workers Act. This bill increases the low-income housing tax credit, the most important resource for creating affordable housing in the United States today, from 9% to 12.5%. It also authorizes State and local agencies to issue tax credits for lower-income housing supply to developers. Urged Housing and Urban Development Secretary Marcia Fudge to approve the Preservation and Reinvestment Initiative for Community Enhancement (PRICE) program to ensure plentiful federal investment and grants for affordable housing. To watch the full event at the Miami City Hall, click here ."
  },
  {
   "id": 124,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT WASHINGTON, D.C. — This week, Congresswoman María Elvira Salazar (R-FL), Congresswoman Elaine Luria (D-VA), Congressman Dan Crenshaw (R-TX), Congressman Joe Neguse (D-CO), and Congressman Garret Graves (R-LA) introduced H.R. 4215 , the bipartisan Rebuilding Communities After Disasters Act with 35 original co-sponsors including:"
  },
  {
   "id": 125,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Ed Case (D-HI), Brian Mas t (R-FL), G.K. Butterfield (D-NC), Carlos Gimenez (R-FL), Eric Swalwell (D-CA), Nicole Malliotakis (R-NY), Charlie Crist (D-FL), Rick Crawford (R-AR), Randy Weber (R-TX), Nancy Mace (R-SC), Troy Nehls (R-TX), Austin Scott (R-GA), Jerry Carl (R-AL), Doug LaMalfa (R-CA), Ashley Hinson (R-IA), Mariannette Miller-Meeks (R-IA), Carol Miller (R-WV), Dave Rouzer (R-NC), Julia Letlow (R-LA), Cathy McMorris Rodgers (R-WA), Clay Higgins (R-LA), Tom Rice (R-SC), Brian Babin (R-TX), Buddy Carter (R-GA), Michael Cloud (R-TX), Rep. David Valadao (R-CA), Greg Murphy (R-NC), Tracey Mann (R-KS), Cliff Bentz (R-OR), Michael Guest (R-MS), and Jenniffer Gonzalez Colon (R-PR)."
  },
  {
   "id": 126,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "The Rebuilding Communities After Disasters A ct ensures homeowners have adequate resources to recover from natural disasters. Specifically, it increases the maximum loan amount for SBA physical damage disaster loans from $200,000 to $400,000 for home repair, and from $40,000 to $75,000 to replace household and personal belongings, bringing the loans limits in line with today’s home prices to help homeowners fully recover from unavoidable disasters. The limits on these loans have not been increased since 1994 - over 25 years - when the average home price in the United States was $106,000."
  },
  {
   "id": 127,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "The bill would also require the SBA to market these loans to homeowners in a declared disaster area through all media platforms and to provide a yearly report to Congress on the progress of the loan program. This bill comes alongside the Small Business Administration's Declaration of Disaster for Surfside victims, which offers these loans to those impacted by the Surfside condo collapse in Miami-Dade County. More information here ."
  },
  {
   "id": 128,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "\"We are in the midst of hurricane season, and in South Florida, we know all too well how these storms can absolutely devastate our homes,\" said Congresswoman Mar í a Elvira Salazar . \"We must do everything possible so that our coastal communities have access to the all resources provided by the SBA to safely rebuild their homes in the event of a disaster. The Disaster Assistance Loans must be modernized to reflect the rising costs of homes across our communities.\""
  },
  {
   "id": 129,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "“In Coastal Virginia, recurrent flooding and extreme weather put homes and property at significant risk of destruction,” said Congresswoman Elaine Luria. “We must ensure local homeowners receive the assistance they need to repair or replace property following natural disasters. I am proud to co-lead the Rebuilding Communities After Disasters Act, which would significantly increase aid to help residents of vulnerable communities recover from the impacts of our changing climate.”"
  },
  {
   "id": 130,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "“This bill will have an immediate impact on families and small businesses impacted by disasters. Many families in Houston have experience the heartbreak and frustration of attempting to rebuild, only to encounter outdated and burdensome relief programs. Modernizing the SBA Disaster Loan Program and increasing the program’s loan limit will go a long way to ensure we are ready for future disasters and will remove barriers for families to rebuild their lives,\" Congressman Dan Crenshaw said."
  },
  {
   "id": 131,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "\"In 2020, Colorado experienced record-setting wildfires with two of the largest in state history burning in the 2nd District. These fires damaged homes, impacted small business operations and forced many in our communities to evacuate with very little notice. As wildfires, flooding and other extreme weather events become more frequent, it is pivotal that our communities have what they need to recover, rebuild and repair,” said Congressman Joe Neguse, Co-Chair of the Bipartisan Wildfire Caucus."
  },
  {
   "id": 132,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "“I’m proud to help introduce the Rebuilding Communities After Disaster Act alongside Congresswoman Salazar today to bring needed federal resources to our families, homeowners and small businesses in the wake of devastating western wildfires. As our communities continue to face the Herculean challenge of these disasters, we will continue to do all we can to find creative solutions, expand resources and equip Colorado.”"
  },
  {
   "id": 133,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "“In the aftermath of disasters, we often find our own federal government fails to be helpful – revictimizing our citizens. Current disaster loan limits fail to address real needs. It is not helpful to offer loans to rebuild part of your home. This legislation increases loan limits for disaster victims to help provide a real solution to rebuilding and recovering. This is a good step forward, but we should never abandon the goal of actually protecting our citizens and preventing disasters from occurring,” Congressman Garret Graves said ."
  },
  {
   "id": 134,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Through its Office of Disaster Assistance (ODA), the Small Business Administration (SBA) has been a major source of assistance for the restoration of commerce and households in areas stricken by natural and human-caused disasters since the agency’s creation in 1953. Through its disaster loan program, SBA offers low-interest, long-term loans for physical and economic damages to businesses to help repair, rebuild, and recover from economic losses after a declared disaster. The majority of the agency’s disaster loans, however (over 80%) are made to individuals and households (renters and property owners) to help repair and replace homes and personal property."
  },
  {
   "id": 135,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Congresswoman Salazar currently represents Florida's beautiful 27th Congressional district which includes most of the City of Miami, its suburbs, and the beaches. She serves on the House Small Business Committee and is the Ranking Member on the Subcommittee on Contracting and Infrastructure. LA REPRESENTANTE SALAZAR PRESENTA LA LEY RECONSTRUCCIÓN DE COMUNIDADES DESPUÉS DE DESASTRES"
  },
  {
   "id": 136,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "WASHINGTON, D.C. - Hoy, la congresista María Elvira Salazar (R-FL), la congresista Elaine Luria (D-VA), el congresista Dan Crenshaw (R-TX), el congresista Joe Neguse (D-CO) y el congresista Garret Graves (R- LA) presentaron H.R. 4215, la ley bipartidista Reconstrucción de Comunidades Después de Desastres con 35 copatrocinadores originales que incluyen los representantes:"
  },
  {
   "id": 137,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Ed Case (D-HI), Brian Mast (R-FL), G.K. Butterfield (D-NC), Carlos Gimenez (R-FL), Eric Swalwell (D-CA), Nicole Malliotakis (R-NY), Charlie Crist (D-FL), Rick Crawford (R-AR), Randy Weber ( R-TX), Nancy Mace (R-SC), Troy Nehls (R-TX), Austin Scott (R-GA), Jerry Carl (R-AL), Doug LaMalfa (R-CA), Ashley Hinson (R- IA), Mariannette Miller-Meeks (R-IA), Carol Miller (R-WV), Dave Rouzer (R-NC), Julia Letlow (R-LA), Cathy McMorris Rodgers (R-WA), Clay Higgins (R -LA), Tom Rice (R-SC), Brian Babin (R-TX), Buddy Carter (R-GA), Michael Cloud (R-TX), David Valadao (R-CA), Greg Murphy (R -NC), Tracey Mann (R-KS), Cliff Bentz (R-OR), Michael Guest (R-MS) y Jenniffer Gonzalez Colon (R-PR)."
  },
  {
   "id": 138,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "La Ley de Reconstrucción de Comunidades Después de Desastres garantiza que los propietarios tengan los recursos adecuados para recuperarse de los desastres naturales. Específicamente, aumenta el monto máximo del préstamo para los préstamos ofrecidos por la Agencia Federal de Pequeños Negocios de EE. UU. (SBA, en inglés) para pagar los costes de daños físicos relacionados con los desastres naturales de $200,000 a $400,000 para reparaciones del hogar, y de $40,000 a $75,000 para reemplazar las pertenencias personales y del hogar."
  },
  {
   "id": 139,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Estos cambios hacen que los límites de préstamos estén en línea con los precios de las viviendas actuales para ayudar a los propietarios a recuperarse por completo de los desastres inevitables. Los límites de estos préstamos no se han incrementado desde 1994, más de 25 años, cuando el precio promedio de la vivienda en los Estados Unidos era de $106,000. El proyecto de ley también requeriría que la SBA comercialice estos préstamos a los propietarios de viviendas en un área declarada desastre a través de todas las plataformas multimedias y proporcione un informe anual al Congreso sobre el progreso del programa de préstamos."
  },
  {
   "id": 140,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Este proyecto de ley viene junto con la declaración de desastre de la SBA para las víctimas de Surfside, que ofrece estos préstamos a los afectados por el colapso de los condominios de Surfside en el condado de Miami-Dade. Más información aquí ."
  },
  {
   "id": 141,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "“Estamos en medio de la temporada de huracanes, y en el sur de la Florida sabemos muy bien cómo estas tormentas pueden devastar absolutamente nuestros hogares,” dijo la congresista María Elvira Salazar . “Debemos hacer todo lo posible para que nuestras comunidades costeras tengan acceso a todos los recursos proporcionados por la SBA para reconstruir de manera segura sus hogares en caso de una tormenta. Los préstamos de asistencia por desastre deben modernizarse para reflejar el aumento de los costes de los hogares en nuestras comunidades.”"
  },
  {
   "id": 142,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "“En la costa de Virginia, las inundaciones recurrentes y el clima extremo ponen las casas y propiedades en un riesgo significativo de destrucción,” dijo la congresista Elaine Luria. “Debemos asegurarnos de que los propietarios de viviendas locales reciban la asistencia que necesitan para reparar o reemplazar la propiedad después de desastres naturales. Me enorgullece ser uno de los líderes de la Ley de Reconstrucción de Comunidades Después de Desastres, que aumentaría significativamente las ayudas para aliviar a los residentes de comunidades vulnerables a recuperarse de los impactos de nuestro clima cambiante.”"
  },
  {
   "id": 143,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "“Este proyecto de ley tendrá un impacto inmediato en las familias y pequeñas empresas afectadas por desastres. Muchas familias en Houston han experimentado la angustia y la frustración de intentar reconstruir, solo para encontrar programas de ayuda obsoletos y onerosos. Modernizar el Programa de Préstamos por Desastres de la SBA y aumentar el límite de préstamos del programa contribuirá en gran medida a garantizar que estemos preparados para desastres futuros y eliminará las barreras para que las familias reconstruyan sus vidas,” dijo el congresista Dan Crenshaw."
  },
  {
   "id": 144,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "“En 2020, Colorado experimentó incendios forestales récord con dos de los más grandes en la historia del estado ardiendo en el Segundo Distrito. Estos incendios dañaron hogares, afectaron las operaciones de pequeñas empresas y obligaron a muchos en nuestras comunidades a evacuar con muy poco aviso. Como los incendios forestales, inundaciones y otros eventos climáticos extremos se vuelven más frecuentes, es fundamental que nuestras comunidades tengan lo que necesitan para recuperarse, reconstruir y reparar,” dijo el congresista Joe Neguse , el también co-presidente del Caucus Bipartidistas de Incendios Forestales."
  },
  {
   "id": 145,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Estoy orgulloso de ayudar a presentar la Ley de Reconstrucción de Comunidades Después de Desastres junto con la Congresista Salazar hoy para llevar los recursos federales necesarios a nuestras familias, propietarios de viviendas y pequeñas empresas a raíz de los devastadores incendios forestales occidentales. Mientras nuestras comunidades continúan enfrentando el desafío hercúleo de estos desastres, continuaremos haciendo todo lo posible para encontrar soluciones creativas, ampliar recursos y equipar a Colorado.”"
  },
  {
   "id": 146,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "“Como secuela de los desastres, encontramos con frecuencia que nuestro propio gobierno federal no es útil, victimizando de nuevo a nuestros ciudadanos. Los límites actuales de préstamos por desastre no satisfacen las necesidades reales. No es útil ofrecer préstamos para reconstruir parte de su casa. Esta legislación aumenta los límites de préstamos para las víctimas de desastres para ayudar a brindar una solución real para la reconstrucción y la recuperación. Este es un buen paso adelante, pero nunca debemos abandonar el objetivo de proteger realmente a nuestros ciudadanos y prevenir que ocurran desastres,” dijo el congresista Garret Graves."
  },
  {
   "id": 147,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "A través de su Oficina de Asistencia para Desastres (ODA), la SBA ha sido una fuente importante de asistencia para la restauración del comercio y los hogares en áreas afectadas por desastres naturales y causados por el hombre desde la creación de la agencia en 1953. A través de su Programa de Préstamos por Desastres, la SBA ofrece préstamos a largo plazo a bajo interés para daños físicos y económicos a empresas para ayudar a reparar, reconstruir y recuperarse de pérdidas económicas después de un desastre declarado."
  },
  {
   "id": 148,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl27-salazar",
   "url": "https://salazar.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-salazar-introduces-rebuilding-communities-after-disasters-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "REP. SALAZAR INTRODUCES THE REBUILDING COMMUNITIES AFTER DISASTERS ACT | Representative Maria Salazar",
   "text": "Sin embargo, la mayoría de los préstamos por desastre de la agencia (más del 80%) se otorgan a individuos y hogares (inquilinos y propietarios) para ayudar a reparar y reemplazar casas y bienes personales. La congresista Salazar representa actualmente el hermoso 27mo distrito congresional de la Florida, que incluye la mayor parte de la ciudad de Miami, sus suburbios y sus playas. Es miembro de la Comisión de Pequeñas Empresas y de la Comisión de Asuntos Exteriores de la Cámara de Representantes."
  },
  {
   "id": 149,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2026/4/congressman-carlos-a-gimenez-releases-statement-on-haiti-temporary-protected-status",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "CONGRESSMAN CARLOS A. GIMENEZ RELEASES STATEMENT ON HAITI TEMPORARY PROTECTED STATUS | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "CONGRESSMAN CARLOS A. GIMENEZ RELEASES STATEMENT ON HAITI TEMPORARY PROTECTED STATUS | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez Resources for American Citizens in Israel CONGRESSMAN CARLOS A. GIMENEZ RELEASES STATEMENT ON HAITI TEMPORARY PROTECTED STATUS WASHINGTON, D.C. - Today, Congressman Carlos A. Gimenez released the following statement after the passage of H.R. 1689 - To require the Secretary of Homeland Security to designate Haiti for temporary protected status:"
  },
  {
   "id": 150,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2026/4/congressman-carlos-a-gimenez-releases-statement-on-haiti-temporary-protected-status",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "CONGRESSMAN CARLOS A. GIMENEZ RELEASES STATEMENT ON HAITI TEMPORARY PROTECTED STATUS | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Congressman Carlos A. Gimenez said, \" I’ve built my record on putting our community first and working across the aisle to get things done. I’m proud of my bipartisan track record—because doing what’s right shouldn’t be about politics, it should be about people. \"Haitian migrants are not strangers—they are our neighbors, our coworkers, and part of the fabric of our community."
  },
  {
   "id": 151,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2026/4/congressman-carlos-a-gimenez-releases-statement-on-haiti-temporary-protected-status",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "CONGRESSMAN CARLOS A. GIMENEZ RELEASES STATEMENT ON HAITI TEMPORARY PROTECTED STATUS | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "\"Haiti today is overrun by violent gangs. It is neither safe nor humane to force our neighbors back into those conditions. Providing Temporary Protected Status (TPS) is not just sound policy—it’s the right thing to do and I’m proud to vote for this commonsense, bipartisan solution that ensures our Haitian neighbors can continue contributing to our community.\" Permalink: https://gimenez.house.gov/2026/4/congressman-carlos-a-gimenez-releases-statement-on-haiti-temporary-protected-status"
  },
  {
   "id": 152,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/congressman-carlos-gimenez-sends-letter-on-tps",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "CONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ SENDS LETTER ON TPS | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "CONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ SENDS LETTER ON TPS | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez Resources for American Citizens in Israel CONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ SENDS LETTER ON TPS MIAMI, FL - Today, Congressman Carlos Gimenez (R-FL) sent a letter to Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem on the current situation of Venezuelan exiles in the United States. Congressman Gimenez is urging Secretary Noem to provide a case-by-case solution to Venezuelan exiles fleeing the communist regime in Venezuela. Congressman Carlos Gimenez represents South Florida, home of the largest Venezuelan exile community in the United States and has been a long-time champion of the Venezuelan community."
  },
  {
   "id": 153,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/congressman-carlos-gimenez-sends-letter-on-tps",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "CONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ SENDS LETTER ON TPS | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Congressman Carlos Gim&eacute;nez represents Miami-Dade County and the beautiful Florida Keys. He is the only Cuban-born Member of the 119th Congress, having fled his homeland shortly after the Communist takeover of the island. He is the first career firefighter paramedic elected to the House of Representatives and served as the former Fire Chief of the City of Miami and Mayor of Miami-Dade County. Rep. Gimenez was appointed by Speaker Mike Johnson to the Smithsonian Institution’s Board of Regents and serves as Vice-Chairman of the Republican Governance Group."
  },
  {
   "id": 154,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/congressman-carlos-gimenez-sends-letter-on-tps",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "CONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ SENDS LETTER ON TPS | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "He serves as the Chairman of the Homeland Security Subcommittee on Transportation and Maritime Security, the Armed Services Committee, and the Select Committee on the Chinese Communist Party. Permalink: https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/congressman-carlos-gimenez-sends-letter-on-tps"
  },
  {
   "id": 155,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/gim-nez-d-az-balart-and-salazar-stand-in-solidarity-with-the-venezuelan-people",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMÉNEZ, DÍAZ-BALART, AND SALAZAR STAND IN SOLIDARITY WITH THE VENEZUELAN PEOPLE | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "GIMÉNEZ, DÍAZ-BALART, AND SALAZAR STAND IN SOLIDARITY WITH THE VENEZUELAN PEOPLE | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez Resources for American Citizens in Israel GIMÉNEZ, DÍAZ-BALART, AND SALAZAR STAND IN SOLIDARITY WITH THE VENEZUELAN PEOPLE MIAMI, FL - Today, Representatives Carlos A. Gim&eacute;nez (FL-28), Mario D&iacute;az-Balart (FL-26), and Mar&iacute;a Elvira Salazar (FL-27), released the following joint statement regarding Temporary Protected Status (TPS) for Venezuelan nationals:"
  },
  {
   "id": 156,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/gim-nez-d-az-balart-and-salazar-stand-in-solidarity-with-the-venezuelan-people",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMÉNEZ, DÍAZ-BALART, AND SALAZAR STAND IN SOLIDARITY WITH THE VENEZUELAN PEOPLE | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "The lawmakers said: \"The regime of Nicol&aacute;s Maduro is one of the world’s most repressive dictatorships, and its mounting failures have led to one of the largest migration crises in history, with millions of Venezuelans being forced to flee the brutal and oppressive regime. \"As a result, many Venezuelans have arrived in our country and have integrated into our communities, respecting our laws and contributing to the prosperity of our great country."
  },
  {
   "id": 157,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/gim-nez-d-az-balart-and-salazar-stand-in-solidarity-with-the-venezuelan-people",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMÉNEZ, DÍAZ-BALART, AND SALAZAR STAND IN SOLIDARITY WITH THE VENEZUELAN PEOPLE | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "\"Unfortunately, we have seen how some individuals, such as members of the Tren de Aragua, have exploited our generosity and flouted our laws, with connections to both the Maduro regime and organized crime. Just today, President Trump signed the “Laken Riley Act,” which provides federal authorities with the necessary tools to enforce the law and prevent these avoidable horrific crimes, such as the tragic case of Laken Riley, who was murdered by a member of the Tren de Aragua. \"In 2021, in one of his final decisions in office, President Trump granted Deferred Enforced Departure (DED) to Venezuelan nationals in the United States, ensuring that those seeking safety in our country."
  },
  {
   "id": 158,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/gim-nez-d-az-balart-and-salazar-stand-in-solidarity-with-the-venezuelan-people",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMÉNEZ, DÍAZ-BALART, AND SALAZAR STAND IN SOLIDARITY WITH THE VENEZUELAN PEOPLE | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "\"President Trump has shown steadfast and unwavering solidarity with the Venezuelan people, including by protecting those fleeing oppression, supporting the courageous democratic opposition, and imposing tough sanctions on the Maduro dictatorship. We will continue to work with the administration toward a foreign policy that protects U.S. national security interests, keeps Americans safe, and defends human rights and democracy while standing up to the dictators in our hemisphere."
  },
  {
   "id": 159,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/gim-nez-d-az-balart-and-salazar-stand-in-solidarity-with-the-venezuelan-people",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMÉNEZ, DÍAZ-BALART, AND SALAZAR STAND IN SOLIDARITY WITH THE VENEZUELAN PEOPLE | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "\"The Venezuelan people have endured repression, corruption, and human rights abuses for far too long in Venezuela, and it is still not safe for many to return. We will continue to do everything possible to ensure that those seeking freedom from persecution and oppression are protected.\" Gim&eacute;nez,D&iacute;az-Balart, y Salazar se solidarizan con el pueblo venezolano MIAMI, FL - Hoy los legisladores Carlos A. Gim&eacute;nez (FL-28), Mario D&iacute;az-Balart (FL-26) y Mar&iacute;a Elvira Salazar (FL-27) emitieron la siguiente declaraci&oacute;n conjunta sobre el Estatus de Protecci&oacute;n Temporal (TPS, por sus siglas en ingl&eacute;s) para los ciudadanos venezolanos:"
  },
  {
   "id": 160,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/gim-nez-d-az-balart-and-salazar-stand-in-solidarity-with-the-venezuelan-people",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMÉNEZ, DÍAZ-BALART, AND SALAZAR STAND IN SOLIDARITY WITH THE VENEZUELAN PEOPLE | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Los legisladores declararon: \"El r&eacute;gimen de Nicol&aacute;s Maduro es una de las dictaduras m&aacute;s represivas del mundo, y sus crecientes fracasos han provocado una de las crisis migratorias m&aacute;s grandes de la historia, con millones de venezolanos siendo forzados a huir del brutal y opresivo r&eacute;gimen. Como resultado, muchos venezolanos han llegado a nuestro pa&iacute;s y se han integrado a nuestras comunidades, respetando nuestras leyes y contribuyendo a la prosperidad de nuestro gran pa&iacute;s."
  },
  {
   "id": 161,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/gim-nez-d-az-balart-and-salazar-stand-in-solidarity-with-the-venezuelan-people",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMÉNEZ, DÍAZ-BALART, AND SALAZAR STAND IN SOLIDARITY WITH THE VENEZUELAN PEOPLE | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Lamentablemente, hemos visto c&oacute;mo algunos individuos, como miembros del Tren de Aragua, han explotado nuestra generosidad y violado nuestras leyes, con v&iacute;nculos tanto con el r&eacute;gimen de Maduro como con el crimen organizado. Justo hoy, el presidente Trump firm&oacute; la “Ley Laken Riley,” que proporciona a las autoridades federales las herramientas necesarias para hacer cumplir la ley y prevenir estos horribles cr&iacute;menes evitables, como el tr&aacute;gico caso de Laken Riley, quien fue asesinada por un miembro del Tren de Aragua."
  },
  {
   "id": 162,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/gim-nez-d-az-balart-and-salazar-stand-in-solidarity-with-the-venezuelan-people",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMÉNEZ, DÍAZ-BALART, AND SALAZAR STAND IN SOLIDARITY WITH THE VENEZUELAN PEOPLE | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "En 2021, en una de sus &uacute;ltimas decisiones de su primer mandato, el presidente Trump otorg&oacute; Salida Forzosa Diferida (DED, por sus siglas en ingl&eacute;s) a los nacionales venezolanos en Estados Unidos, asegurando que aquellos que buscan seguridad en nuestro pa&iacute;s no ser&aacute;n deportados de vuelta a la dictadura, donde podr&iacute;an enfrentar persecuci&oacute;n, abusos de derechos humanos e incluso la muerte."
  },
  {
   "id": 163,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/gim-nez-d-az-balart-and-salazar-stand-in-solidarity-with-the-venezuelan-people",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMÉNEZ, DÍAZ-BALART, AND SALAZAR STAND IN SOLIDARITY WITH THE VENEZUELAN PEOPLE | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "El presidente Trump ha mostrado una solidaridad firme e inquebrantable con el pueblo venezolano, incluyendo la protecci&oacute;n de aquellos que huyen de la opresi&oacute;n, el apoyo a la valiente oposici&oacute;n democr&aacute;tica, y la imposici&oacute;n de sanciones contundentes contra la dictadura de Maduro. Continuaremos trabajando con la Administraci&oacute;n hacia una pol&iacute;tica exterior que proteja los intereses de seguridad nacional de los EE.UU., mantenga a los americanos seguros y defienda los derechos humanos y la democracia, mientras enfrentamos a los dictadores en nuestro hemisferio."
  },
  {
   "id": 164,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/gim-nez-d-az-balart-and-salazar-stand-in-solidarity-with-the-venezuelan-people",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMÉNEZ, DÍAZ-BALART, AND SALAZAR STAND IN SOLIDARITY WITH THE VENEZUELAN PEOPLE | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "El pueblo venezolano ha soportado represi&oacute;n, corrupci&oacute;n y abusos a los derechos humanos durante demasiado tiempo en Venezuela, y a&uacute;n no es seguro para muchos regresar. Continuaremos haciendo todo lo posible para garantizar que aquellos que buscan libertad por la persecuci&oacute;n y la opresi&oacute;n est&eacute;n protegidos.”"
  },
  {
   "id": 165,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/gim-nez-d-az-balart-and-salazar-stand-in-solidarity-with-the-venezuelan-people",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMÉNEZ, DÍAZ-BALART, AND SALAZAR STAND IN SOLIDARITY WITH THE VENEZUELAN PEOPLE | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "He serves as the Chairman of the Homeland Security Subcommittee on Transportation and Maritime Security, the Armed Services Committee, and the Select Committee on the Chinese Communist Party. Permalink: https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/1/gim-nez-d-az-balart-and-salazar-stand-in-solidarity-with-the-venezuelan-people"
  },
  {
   "id": 166,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2021/3/gimenez-biden-administration-giving-tps-venezuelan-nationals-living-united",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Gimenez on Biden Administration giving TPS to Venezuelan nationals living in the United States | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Gimenez on Biden Administration giving TPS to Venezuelan nationals living in the United States | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez Resources for American Citizens in Israel Gimenez on Biden Administration giving TPS to Venezuelan nationals living in the United States WASHINGTON, D.C. – Congressman Carlos A. Gimenez issued the following statement after the Biden Administration announced the establishment of Temporary Protected Status (TPS) for Venezuelan nationals living in the United States:"
  },
  {
   "id": 167,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2021/3/gimenez-biden-administration-giving-tps-venezuelan-nationals-living-united",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Gimenez on Biden Administration giving TPS to Venezuelan nationals living in the United States | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "“I applaud the decision by President Biden and his national security team for establishing TPS for Venezuelans. Countless Venezuelan nationals live in my district, most fleeing from the scourge of communism and fearing for their lives. They have found a home in America, one where they can express themselves freely without fear of political retribution and where they can work to fulfill their God-given potential. “Nicolás Maduro and his criminal communist regime have stolen the wealth, obliterated the civil rights, persecuted, and tortured the people of Venezuela, forcing millions to leave their homeland seeking the freedom and security that they cannot find in his own nation."
  },
  {
   "id": 168,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2021/3/gimenez-biden-administration-giving-tps-venezuelan-nationals-living-united",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Gimenez on Biden Administration giving TPS to Venezuelan nationals living in the United States | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "\\r\\n“I hope that the Biden administration will continue taking actions in favor of the democracy in the region and will not give concessions to the criminal regimes of Havana and Caracas. I extend my recognition to congressman and my friend Mario Diaz-Balart for his constant commitment to ensure that our Venezuelan community could achieve this important goal.” Permalink: https://gimenez.house.gov/2021/3/gimenez-biden-administration-giving-tps-venezuelan-nationals-living-united"
  },
  {
   "id": 169,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/1/gimenez-rubio-reintroduce-the-south-florida-ecosystem-enhancement-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ, RUBIO REINTRODUCE THE SOUTH FLORIDA ECOSYSTEM ENHANCEMENT ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "GIMENEZ, RUBIO REINTRODUCE THE SOUTH FLORIDA ECOSYSTEM ENHANCEMENT ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez Resources for American Citizens in Israel GIMENEZ, RUBIO REINTRODUCE THE SOUTH FLORIDA ECOSYSTEM ENHANCEMENT ACT WASHINGTON D.C - Congressman Carlos A. Gimenez (FL-28) reintroduced the South Florida Ecosystem Enhancement Act, which reauthorizes and reforms the South Florida Geographic Program (SFGP) to support ecosystem restoration and monitoring efforts across the contiguous aquatic ecosystems of southern Florida. Florida Senator Marco Rubio introduced companion legislation in the Senate. Upon introducing the bill in the House, Gimenez said:"
  },
  {
   "id": 170,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/1/gimenez-rubio-reintroduce-the-south-florida-ecosystem-enhancement-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ, RUBIO REINTRODUCE THE SOUTH FLORIDA ECOSYSTEM ENHANCEMENT ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "“ South Florida includes some of the nation's most rich ecosystems expanding from the Everglades to the Florida Keys. It’s an honor to partner with Senator Marco Rubio to introduce the South Florida Ecosystem Enhancement Act. Our bill reauthorizes the South Florida Geographic Program and helps get much needed money to South Florida ecological restoration projects. These projects will help preserve South Florida’s precious ecosystems for generations to come .” After introducing the bill in the Senate, Rubio said:"
  },
  {
   "id": 171,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/1/gimenez-rubio-reintroduce-the-south-florida-ecosystem-enhancement-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ, RUBIO REINTRODUCE THE SOUTH FLORIDA ECOSYSTEM ENHANCEMENT ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "“ Restoring South Florida’s ecosystems is crucial because these habitats are the beating heart of Florida’s lifestyle and economy, ” Rubio said . “ Reauthorizing the South Florida Geographic Program is an important step to restoring these unique habitats. ” The South Florida Ecosystem Enhancement Act is supported by Audubon Florida, the Bonefish & Tarpon Trust, the Coastal and Heartland National Estuary Partnership, the Everglades Foundation, the Indian River Lagoon National Estuary Program, and the Sanibel-Captiva Conservation Foundation."
  },
  {
   "id": 172,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/1/gimenez-rubio-reintroduce-the-south-florida-ecosystem-enhancement-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ, RUBIO REINTRODUCE THE SOUTH FLORIDA ECOSYSTEM ENHANCEMENT ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "“ This is a historic investment in the South Florida Geographic Program. We applaud Senator Rubio and Representative Gimenez for their commitment to reauthorizing this important effort to advance conservation goals across the South Florida footprint .” – Julie Wraithmell, Executive Director of Audubon Florida"
  },
  {
   "id": 173,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/1/gimenez-rubio-reintroduce-the-south-florida-ecosystem-enhancement-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ, RUBIO REINTRODUCE THE SOUTH FLORIDA ECOSYSTEM ENHANCEMENT ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "“ Reauthorization of the South Florida Ecosystem Enhancement Act and the amendments to the South Florida Geographic Program proposed by Senator Rubio and Congressman Gimenez will continue to fund much needed water quality and habitat restoration projects that are helping to restore our south Florida coastal ecosystems .” – Dr. Duane DeFreese, Executive Director, Indian River Lagoon National Estuary Program"
  },
  {
   "id": 174,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/1/gimenez-rubio-reintroduce-the-south-florida-ecosystem-enhancement-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ, RUBIO REINTRODUCE THE SOUTH FLORIDA ECOSYSTEM ENHANCEMENT ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "“ The Coastal & Heartland National Estuary Partnership strongly supports the reauthorization of the South Florida Geographic Program (SFGP), which will be accomplished through the South Florida Ecosystem Enhancement Act. This legislation that Senator Rubio and Congressman Gimenez have introduced will provide $50 million dollars of funding per year over the next 5 years; critically needed resources to protecting water and wildlife, as well as the Everglades – a national treasure. Passage of it will create transformational results in enhancing South Florida’s economy and quality of life as well .” – Jennifer Hecker, Executive Director, Coastal and Heartland National Estuary Partnership"
  },
  {
   "id": 175,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/1/gimenez-rubio-reintroduce-the-south-florida-ecosystem-enhancement-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ, RUBIO REINTRODUCE THE SOUTH FLORIDA ECOSYSTEM ENHANCEMENT ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "“ Clean water and healthy habitat are vital for our fisheries. We are grateful to Senator Rubio and Representative Gimenez for introducing the South Florida Ecosystem Enhancement Act to reauthorize and update the South Florida Geographic Program. This program has played an important role in improving South Florida ecosystems, and expansion of this program to include the Indian River Lagoon and Charlotte Harbor National Estuary Programs, along with providing funding opportunities and coordination with the South Florida Ecosystem Restoration Task Force will deliver even more benefits to Florida’s iconic natural resources."
  },
  {
   "id": 176,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/1/gimenez-rubio-reintroduce-the-south-florida-ecosystem-enhancement-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ, RUBIO REINTRODUCE THE SOUTH FLORIDA ECOSYSTEM ENHANCEMENT ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "” – Kellie Ralston, Vice President for Conservation and Public Policy with the Bonefish & Tarpon Trust “ The reauthorization of this important program will support much-needed grant opportunities for ecosystem restoration and monitoring efforts by state, local, and tribal governments as well as non-governmental organizations within the SFGP boundaries. ” – James Evans, Chief Executive Officer, Sanibel-Captiva Conservation Foundation The South Florida Ecosystem Enhancement Act: Reauthorizes the South Florida Geographic Program (SFGP) for fiscal years 2024-2028;"
  },
  {
   "id": 177,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/1/gimenez-rubio-reintroduce-the-south-florida-ecosystem-enhancement-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ, RUBIO REINTRODUCE THE SOUTH FLORIDA ECOSYSTEM ENHANCEMENT ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Integrates the Geographic Program authority into the Clean Water Act, which houses the authorities for other geographic programs such as the Great Lakes Geographic Program, Chesapeake Bay Geographic Program, and Columbia River Geographic Program; Expands the geographic scope of the SFGP to include the study areas of the Coastal and Heartland National Estuary Partnership and the Indian River Lagoon National Estuary Program (large portions of which already fall inside the current SFGP study area) to better coordinate restoration and monitoring efforts in these contiguous ecosystems;"
  },
  {
   "id": 178,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/1/gimenez-rubio-reintroduce-the-south-florida-ecosystem-enhancement-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ, RUBIO REINTRODUCE THE SOUTH FLORIDA ECOSYSTEM ENHANCEMENT ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Establishes a grant program to make funding opportunities available for ecosystem restoration and monitoring efforts by state, local, and tribal governments, as well as nongovernmental organizations within the boundaries of the SFGP; Directs the SFGP Senior Advisor to solicit priority projects and activities from the South Florida Ecosystem Restoration (SFER) Task Force and authorizes the Senior Advisor to enter into interagency agreements and cooperative agreements with federal, state, local, and tribal entities to carry out those projects and activities; and"
  },
  {
   "id": 179,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/1/gimenez-rubio-reintroduce-the-south-florida-ecosystem-enhancement-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ, RUBIO REINTRODUCE THE SOUTH FLORIDA ECOSYSTEM ENHANCEMENT ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Establishes an education grant program to facilitate efforts to improve environmental literacy education, with a priority focus on funding field trips for socially disadvantaged students in public K-12 schools to facilitate access to publicly protected lands and natural resources. Permalink: https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/1/gimenez-rubio-reintroduce-the-south-florida-ecosystem-enhancement-act"
  },
  {
   "id": 180,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2024/4/rep-carlos-gimenez-introduces-bill-to-enhance-coral-restoration-efforts",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Rep. Carlos Gimenez Introduces Bill to Enhance Coral Restoration Efforts | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Rep. Carlos Gimenez Introduces Bill to Enhance Coral Restoration Efforts | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez Resources for American Citizens in Israel Rep. Carlos Gimenez Introduces Bill to Enhance Coral Restoration Efforts WASHINGTON, D.C. - Today, Congressman Carlos A. Gimenez (FL-28) and Rep. Debbie Wasserman Schultz (FL-25) co-lead a bill to enhance coral restoration efforts in South Florida. The Conserving Our Reefs Along Lower (CORAL) Florida Act would create a new $5 million grant program to states, local municipalities, non-profits, and non-governmental organizations including the Mote Marine Laboratory in the Florida Keys, to carry out coral restoration efforts."
  },
  {
   "id": 181,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2024/4/rep-carlos-gimenez-introduces-bill-to-enhance-coral-restoration-efforts",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Rep. Carlos Gimenez Introduces Bill to Enhance Coral Restoration Efforts | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "“South Florida’s coral reefs are crucial to our vibrant coastline, support our rich and diverse marine life and aquatic ecosystem, and attract millions of tourists to our great state,” said Rep. Gimenez . “Proud to work on this bipartisan effort to ensure Florida’s reef managers, scientists, and conservation organizations have the resources they need to carry out their critical mission of saving our reefs.”"
  },
  {
   "id": 182,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2024/4/rep-carlos-gimenez-introduces-bill-to-enhance-coral-restoration-efforts",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Rep. Carlos Gimenez Introduces Bill to Enhance Coral Restoration Efforts | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "“Florida’s coral reefs support diverse marine life, protect our coastlines from flooding, and help attract millions of visitors and billions of dollars in economic impact to our state,” said Congresswoman Wasserman Schultz . “Ensuring the health of our beautiful coral reefs is not a partisan issue, it’s a Florida issue, and one with global health implications. I’m proud to be a part of this bipartisan effort to restore South Florida’s aquatic ecosystems.”"
  },
  {
   "id": 183,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2024/4/rep-carlos-gimenez-introduces-bill-to-enhance-coral-restoration-efforts",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Rep. Carlos Gimenez Introduces Bill to Enhance Coral Restoration Efforts | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Congressman Carlos Gim&eacute;nez represents Miami-Dade County and the beautiful Florida Keys. He is the only Cuban-born Member of the 118th Congress, having fled his homeland shortly after the Communist takeover of the island. He is the first career firefighter paramedic elected to the House of Representatives and served as the former Fire Chief of the City of Miami and Mayor of Miami-Dade County. He serves on the House Armed Services Committee, the Homeland Security Committee, and the Select Committee on China. Permalink: https://gimenez.house.gov/2024/4/rep-carlos-gimenez-introduces-bill-to-enhance-coral-restoration-efforts"
  },
  {
   "id": 184,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/2/congressman-carlos-gimenez-introduces-the-national-emergency-declaration-reform-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "CONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ INTRODUCES THE NATIONAL EMERGENCY DECLARATION REFORM ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "CONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ INTRODUCES THE NATIONAL EMERGENCY DECLARATION REFORM ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez Resources for American Citizens in Israel CONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ INTRODUCES THE NATIONAL EMERGENCY DECLARATION REFORM ACT WASHINGTON D.C - Today, Congressman Carlos Gimenez (FL-28) introduced the National Emergency Declaration Reform Act , which would require both houses of Congress to vote every six months to determine whether a National Emergency Declaration should remain in effect."
  },
  {
   "id": 185,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/2/congressman-carlos-gimenez-introduces-the-national-emergency-declaration-reform-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "CONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ INTRODUCES THE NATIONAL EMERGENCY DECLARATION REFORM ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "In the past two years, President Biden’s executive branch has abused the powers of the executive office to use the Covid Emergency Declaration to suspend student loan payment deadlines, to close ports of entry, to expand federal agencies, and to lawlessly cancel student loans all without the approval of Congress. “ We have given way too much power to the executive branch and unelected bureaucrats. The power must be handed back to the people through their elected representatives. I am proud to introduce the National Emergency Declaration Reform Act to ensure both houses of Congress will vote and represent the interests of the American people , said Congressman Gimenez."
  },
  {
   "id": 186,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/2/congressman-carlos-gimenez-introduces-the-national-emergency-declaration-reform-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "CONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ INTRODUCES THE NATIONAL EMERGENCY DECLARATION REFORM ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Over the past two years we have watched President Biden overreach his power with the use of the Covid Emergency Declaration with few to no checks from Congress. The executive branch, no matter the party, should never be able to abuse its power. “"
  },
  {
   "id": 187,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/2/congressman-carlos-gimenez-introduces-the-national-emergency-declaration-reform-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "CONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ INTRODUCES THE NATIONAL EMERGENCY DECLARATION REFORM ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "In September 2022, President Biden said, “The pandemic is over, we still have a problem with COVID… but the pandemic is over.” Yet, six months later we are still under an emergency declaration. The current law for Emergency Declarations is they typically last for one year after declared, until the President declares the emergency is over, or until the House and the Senate vote on a joint resolution terminating the emergency. Each House can consider termination every six months but is not required by law to do so."
  },
  {
   "id": 188,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/2/congressman-carlos-gimenez-introduces-the-national-emergency-declaration-reform-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "CONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ INTRODUCES THE NATIONAL EMERGENCY DECLARATION REFORM ACT | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Congressman Gimenez serves on the House Armed Services Committee, Homeland Security Committee, and the Select Committee on China. He represents Florida’s 28th Congressional District based in Miami-Dade County and the Florida Keys. Congressman Gimenez is the former Mayor of Miami-Dade County and currently the only Cuban-born Member of the 118th Congress. Permalink: https://gimenez.house.gov/2023/2/congressman-carlos-gimenez-introduces-the-national-emergency-declaration-reform-act"
  },
  {
   "id": 189,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2022/3/gimenez-secures-23-7-million-for-south-florida",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ SECURES $23.7 MILLION FOR SOUTH FLORIDA | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "GIMENEZ SECURES $23.7 MILLION FOR SOUTH FLORIDA | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez Resources for American Citizens in Israel GIMENEZ SECURES $23.7 MILLION FOR SOUTH FLORIDA WASHINGTON, D.C. - Congressman Carlos A. Gimenez (FL-26) announced today that his congressional office secured over $23.7 million in funding for Florida’s 26th Congressional District. Each community project funding request submitted by Gimenez’s office was approved, leaving his office with a 100% track record in securing critical funding for South Florida."
  },
  {
   "id": 190,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2022/3/gimenez-secures-23-7-million-for-south-florida",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ SECURES $23.7 MILLION FOR SOUTH FLORIDA | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "“One of the most important functions in my role as a Member of Congress is ensuring that Florida’s 26th Congressional District gets the funding it needs to support critical infrastructure projects and the work of our community’s non-profit organizations. I want to thank my colleague Congressman Mario Diaz-Balart, who serves on the House Appropriations Committee, for his help in ensuring this important funding to South Florida was included in the bill,” Gimenez said. Following Gimenez’s earmark requests in April, this particular appropriations bill includes funding for the following: &middot; Miami-Dade Police Department for Operation Safe Ride , Miami, FL : $2.01 million"
  },
  {
   "id": 191,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2022/3/gimenez-secures-23-7-million-for-south-florida",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ SECURES $23.7 MILLION FOR SOUTH FLORIDA | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "&middot; Florida Keys Water Improvement , Key West, FL : $6 million &middot; Key West Housing Authority , Key West, FL : $2.5 million &middot; Agape Network , Miami, FL : $3 million &middot; Coral Reef Observatory , Miami, FL : $1.14 million &middot; Clean Water State Revolving Fund, Miami-Dade County, FL : $2 million &middot; Twin Lakes Pre-Disaster Mitigation , Monroe County, FL : $5.4 million &middot; Homestead Police Department Body Cameras, Homestead, FL : $750,000 &middot; Employ Miami-Dade , Miami, FL : $500,000 &middot; Miami SCI Wellness , Miami, FL : $440,000"
  },
  {
   "id": 192,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2022/3/gimenez-secures-23-7-million-for-south-florida",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ SECURES $23.7 MILLION FOR SOUTH FLORIDA | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "“Operation Safe Ride provides robust services by the Miami-Dade Police Department on public transit, ensuring that travelers in and throughout the Miami metropolitan area have ride our public transit systems safely. This money will help keep our communities and our families safer while encouraging the use of Miami’s public transit,” Gimenez said. “This funding will help protect and improve the near shore waters of the National Marine Sanctuary, helping to ensure that the Florida Keys continues to be a robust economic powerhouse in South Florida,” Gimenez said."
  },
  {
   "id": 193,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2022/3/gimenez-secures-23-7-million-for-south-florida",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ SECURES $23.7 MILLION FOR SOUTH FLORIDA | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "“With this funding, the Key West Housing Authority will have the ability to replace an aging transformer and generator, helping maintain necessary functions at the Senior Citizen Plaza in the event of a blackout. Due to the location of Key West in the Caribbean Sea, the island is subject to a volatile and uncertain weather pattern, especially during the Hurricane Season. This project will directly benefit nearly 200 low-income senior families,” Gimenez said."
  },
  {
   "id": 194,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2022/3/gimenez-secures-23-7-million-for-south-florida",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "GIMENEZ SECURES $23.7 MILLION FOR SOUTH FLORIDA | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "“For many residents, the Agape Network is a crucial component of Miami’s health care industry. This funding would help the organization construct the Agape Village Health Center, a project that will double the number of weekly outpatient services it can provide and create space for 121 new employees,” Gimenez said. “This money will be greatly beneficial for the Aquarius Coral Reef Observatory at Florida International University. Coral reefs are an incredibly important part of South Florida’s ecosystem and more needs to be done to not only preserve them for our future generations, but also learn more about their important functions to our ecosystem,” Gimenez said."
