   "title": "Diaz-Balart Delivers Another Year of Record Level Investment in Infrastructure and Housing | Congressman Mario Diaz-Balart",
   "text": "$465 million for the Payment in Lieu of Taxes program, which Collier County is the largest recipient in Florida of $68 million to support critical water infrastructure projects through the Water Infrastructure Finance and Innovation Act (WIFIA) $1.01 billion for the Animal and Plant Health Inspection Services to combat plant and animal pests and diseases, including citrus greening $819 million for Natural Resources Conservation Services $625 million for infrastructure investments in Rural America $73.477 billion for Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP) State, Foreign Operations, and Related Programs"
  },
  {
   "id": 428,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl26-diaz-balart",
   "url": "https://mariodiazbalart.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/diaz-balart-delivers-another-year-record-level-investment",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Diaz-Balart Delivers Another Year of Record Level Investment in Infrastructure and Housing | Congressman Mario Diaz-Balart",
   "text": "$17.5 under Economic Support Fund for programs to promote democracy and the rule of law in Venezuela $3.3 billion for Israel, fulfilling the U.S. commitment under the Memorandum of Understanding $275 million for the Countering Russian Influence Fund $1.37 billion for the U.S. Agency for International Development (USAID) Financial Services and General Government $250 million to support financial institutions in low-income communities through the Community Development Financial Institution (CDFI) Fund $3 million for CDFIs to provide technical and financial assistance to individuals with disabilities"
  },
  {
   "id": 429,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl26-diaz-balart",
   "url": "https://mariodiazbalart.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/diaz-balart-delivers-another-year-record-level-investment",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Diaz-Balart Delivers Another Year of Record Level Investment in Infrastructure and Housing | Congressman Mario Diaz-Balart",
   "text": "$37.5 billion to help small business owners through the Small Business Administration's 7(a) and 504 loan programs $131 million to support entrepreneurs through Small Business Development Centers $4.9 billion for airport security through the Transportation Security Administration (TSA) $14.9 billion for the U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP) $100 million for new border security technology $77 million for opioid detection equipment to better help CBP officers stop the flow of drugs into our country $16.6 billion for the Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA) $262.5 million for FEMA Flood Hazard Mapping $250 million for pre-disaster mitigation fund"
  },
  {
   "id": 430,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl26-diaz-balart",
   "url": "https://mariodiazbalart.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/diaz-balart-hb-851-allows-young-men-women-reach-god-given-potential",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Diaz-Balart: HB 851 Allows Young Men & Women to Reach God-Given Potential | Congressman Mario Diaz-Balart",
   "text": "Diaz-Balart: HB 851 Allows Young Men & Women to Reach God-Given Potential | Congressman Mario Diaz-Balart Diaz-Balart: HB 851 Allows Young Men & Women to Reach God-Given Potential WASHINGTON – Congressman Mario Diaz-Balart (R-FL) released the following statement in response to the passage of HB 851, the Postsecondary Student Tuition bill, by the Florida State Legislature."
  },
  {
   "id": 431,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl26-diaz-balart",
   "url": "https://mariodiazbalart.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/diaz-balart-hb-851-allows-young-men-women-reach-god-given-potential",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Diaz-Balart: HB 851 Allows Young Men & Women to Reach God-Given Potential | Congressman Mario Diaz-Balart",
   "text": "\"I commend and congratulate the Florida Legislature for passing this important piece of legislation. One of the things that defines the United States is that we are a meritocracy – we judge people not by the actions of their relatives, but by their individual merits. This bill allows young men and women who have done everything society has asked of them to seek a degree of higher education and reach their God-given potential. I thank Speaker Weatherford, Senator Latvala, Representative Nuñez, Governor Scott, and the entire South Florida State Legislature delegation for their leadership on this issue.\""
  },
  {
   "id": 432,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Home - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "Learn More About Te's Affordable Housing Plan Read Te's Plan To Eliminate the H-1B Program Read Te's Plan to Keep Promises to Veterans Read Te's Plan To Defend Our Traditional Values Te Brown is a real estate developer, small businesswoman, and homeschooling mom. She grew up on the tough streets of Chicago and relied on her Christian values and faith in America to build a successful business from scratch. She is a pro-MAGA, pro-Constitution conservative who isn’t afraid to stand up for what’s right. Join the team—knock doors, deliver signs, and help spread the word in FL-24. Explore Te's priorities on healthcare, economy, rural America, and homeownership."
  },
  {
   "id": 433,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Home - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "Chip in to support Te's campaign for Florida's 24th District. Stay updated with the latest news and insights from Te Brown's campaign. Stay tuned for the latest campaign updates and news. Join the team at upcoming events and meet Te Brown at events around the district. We're planning exciting events across the district. For my family and yours, I will fight the Democrats’ radical, anti-American, anti-family agenda that’s trying to destroy our country!"
  },
  {
   "id": 434,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/issues/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "On The Issues - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "Te Brown supports redirecting federal housing dollars away from lifelong rental subsidies and toward helping low-income families in our district buy their first home. Instead of keeping hardworking Americans trapped as permanent renters, housing policy should help families build stability, equity, and independence. It is time to move beyond dependency and give more families the chance to own a piece of the American Dream."
  },
  {
   "id": 435,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/issues/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "On The Issues - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "Every child in Florida’s 24th District deserves a quality education, not a zip code assignment. Te Brown supports taking federal education dollars that currently prop up failing schools and putting that money directly in the hands of parents by funding students, not systems. Families should be empowered to choose the best learning environment for their children, whether that is a public school, charter school, private school, or homeschool. No child should be trapped in an underperforming school because of where their family lives."
  },
  {
   "id": 436,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/issues/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "On The Issues - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "The H-1B program should serve America’s workforce—not be used to undercut American workers’ wages or replace qualified Americans. I support reforms that prioritize American workers, require employers to pay competitive wages, crack down on abuse, and reserve H-1B visas for legitimate high-skill workforce needs where American workers cannot fill the position. No wage suppression or worker replacement H-1B visas for genuine high-skill workforce shortages The men and women who served this country deserve more than empty thank-yous. Faster care, real mental health support, and full accountability at the VA — that’s what our veterans have earned. SECURE BORDERS & A LEGAL IMMIGRATION SYSTEM"
  },
  {
   "id": 437,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/issues/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "On The Issues - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "A nation must have secure borders and a fair, lawful immigration system. I support securing our southern border, enforcing our immigration laws, and prioritizing the removal of criminals and those who pose a threat to public safety. At the same time, we should create a clear, lawful process for people who have earned the right to remain, while ending policies that encourage illegal immigration and ensuring that those who follow the rules are not left behind. Faith, family, and freedom are the foundation of America. Religious liberty, parental rights, the Second Amendment, and the Constitution itself are under attack — and they’re worth fighting for."
  },
  {
   "id": 438,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/issues/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "On The Issues - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "For 15 years, Washington has told Haitian families in South Florida that their status was temporary, and for 15 years nothing changed. During that time, the situation in Haiti has only worsened, and many community members have built businesses, raised families, staffed hospitals, and created institutions the rest of us depend on. Put simply, that is not a temporary population, and the community has earned better than a deportation notice."
  },
  {
   "id": 439,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/issues/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "On The Issues - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "In Congress, I will fight for an earned path to citizenship. Earned: a steady work history, taxes paid, a clean record, a full background check. Not amnesty, and not a cut ahead of anyone who waited in line. A Republican Congress did this in 1998 with the Haitian Refugee Immigration Fairness Act, and it was right then. Those who have worked, paid taxes, built our communities, and embodied the American experience should not be cast aside, but welcomed as who they are: Haitian-Americans."
  },
  {
   "id": 440,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/issues/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "On The Issues - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "I won’t pretend, either, that the other side doesn’t matter. No immigration bill can fix the status of Port-Au-Prince and Haiti. I will work to end the South Florida weapons pipeline to Port-Au-Prince, and back the effort to rebuild, because nobody wants a stable Haiti more than those forced to leave it."
  },
  {
   "id": 441,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/the-people-first-agenda/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "The People First Agenda - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "The People First Agenda - Te Brown For Congress Putting People Before Politics. Delivering Results That Matter. A bold agenda focused on lowering the cost of living, making housing and childcare more affordable, protecting seniors and veterans, creating jobs, protecting the healthcare system, strengthening communities, and putting families first. 1. Affordability & Homeownership — Lower the barriers to buying a home, build more affordable housing, and address the cost of living. 2. Healthcare That Works — Increase transparency, lower prescription and healthcare costs, and protect patients from unnecessary costs."
  },
  {
   "id": 442,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/the-people-first-agenda/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "The People First Agenda - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "3. Jobs & Economic Opportunity — Support small businesses, attract manufacturing, and create good-paying jobs in the district. 4. Infrastructure & Resilience — Invest in roads, bridges, water systems, drainage, and infrastructure that keeps South Florida moving. 5. Protecting Seniors & Veterans — Protect Social Security and Medicare while making sure veterans receive the services they’ve earned. 6. Safe & Strong Communities — Support law enforcement, address crime, and make communities safer. 7. Education & Opportunity — Expand educational choices and make sure children have pathways to careers, trades, college, or entrepreneurship."
  },
  {
   "id": 443,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/the-people-first-agenda/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "The People First Agenda - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "8. Accountability in Washington — Make government live within its means, eliminate waste, and demand measurable results Your concerns are not just messages—they’re the issues I intend to fight to address. Send me your concerns, ideas, and priorities. Together, we can build a People’s First Agenda that delivers results. Email me your concerns and ideas at info@tmbrownforcongress.com"
  },
  {
   "id": 444,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/meet-te-brown/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Meet Te Brown - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "Te Mayonna Brown is the Republican nominee for Florida’s 24th Congressional District. A successful businesswoman, educator, and trailblazing real estate developer, she has spent her career building stronger communities, creating opportunities, and helping families achieve the American Dream. As a woman real estate developer, Te has transformed neighborhoods through affordable housing and economic investment. Her work has given her firsthand experience solving real-world challenges, creating jobs, and helping communities grow."
  },
  {
   "id": 445,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/meet-te-brown/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Meet Te Brown - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "Te also understands the importance of education. As a former teacher, she believes every child deserves access to a quality education and that parents—not government bureaucrats—should have the freedom to choose the best educational path for their children. She is a strong advocate for school choice and policies that put students and families first."
  },
  {
   "id": 446,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/meet-te-brown/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Meet Te Brown - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "Now, Te is taking her experience as a builder, educator, and entrepreneur to Washington. She isn’t a career politician—she’s a proven leader who knows how to get results. She is committed to fighting for stronger wage growth, affordable housing, lower costs for working families, safer communities, and policies that encourage businesses to grow and create better-paying jobs. Te believes America is strongest when government is limited, communities are safe, the economy is growing, and every family has the opportunity to succeed through hard work."
  },
  {
   "id": 447,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/meet-te-brown/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Meet Te Brown - Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "As your next representative in Congress, Te Mayonna Brown will be a strong voice for economic growth, public safety, fiscal responsibility, individual freedom, and common-sense leadership. She will work every day to protect taxpayers, support small businesses, strengthen families, and ensure the next generation has even greater opportunities than the last. Together, we can build a stronger Florida, a stronger economy, and a brighter future for the families of Florida’s 24th Congressional District."
  },
  {
   "id": 448,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-brown",
   "url": "https://tebrownforflorida.com/news/",
   "kind": "campaign_news",
   "title": "News – Te Brown For Congress",
   "text": "Check back soon for the latest updates and announcements from the campaign. Subscribe to our newsletter for the latest campaign updates. No upcoming events to show at this time."
  },
  {
   "id": 449,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "By providing your cell phone number you consent to receive periodic campaign updates from Oliver Gilbert for Congress. Texting & data rates may apply. Reply \"STOP\" to stop texts. Reply \"HELP\" for help. I consent to receive SMS messages from Oliver Gilbert for Congress. Message & data rates may apply, Reply \"STOP\" to stop texts, reply \"help\" for help Rooted in Miami Gardens and shaped by the people who raised him, taught him, and stood by him, Oliver Gilbert is running to give back to the community that made him who he is. Raised in Miami Gardens, educated in local public schools, and shaped by a lifetime of service to his community, he is running to build a stronger future for South Florida."
  },
  {
   "id": 450,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "His story is one of faith, perseverance, and service — from supporting himself as a college student and riding the bus to law school, to leading his growing hometown as Mayor and bringing safer neighborhoods, more parks, real economic growth, to fighting as a County Commissioner for better public transit, housing people can afford, and economic growth that benefits the entire region — his focus has always been on creating stronger neighborhoods, more resilient communities, and a better future for working families. At every step, his purpose has remained the same: to bring opportunity home and build a South Florida where every family has a fair shot."
  },
  {
   "id": 451,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "They want to get to work without losing half their day. They want to see a doctor without dreading the bill. They want their kids to inherit an economy that rewards effort. A two-hour commute isn’t a transit problem. It’s a family problem, a cost problem, and a life problem. Nobody should wait until it’s too late to see a doctor because of the bill. Coverage isn’t a luxury. It’s a foundation. Small businesses and working families built South Florida. They deserve a federal government that builds with them — not around them. and build a brighter future for everyone in South Florida Eliminate Income Taxes for Working Families"
  },
  {
   "id": 452,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Startup grants and affordable financing to get your idea off the ground. The SBA Growth Line offers low-interest loans to help you scale up. A strengthened SBA 504 program makes buying property and expanding easier. Employee ownership and profit-sharing incentives that help workers build wealth. Less paperwork, simpler reporting, and faster approvals for small businesses. Small Business Opportunity Zones that revitalize local commercial corridors. Oliver is relying on the grassroots support of voters like you. Will you make a secure online donation today? This is the most meaningful endorsement I could ask for."
  },
  {
   "id": 453,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Congresswoman Wilson has fought for this community for decades, the last 15 years in Congress doing the hard work to move our community and country forward and she does not give her word lightly. She knows better than anyone what’s needed in Washington. I grew up right here in South Florida, in Miami Gardens. I know what families here are up against, because I have lived it. Rent that eats half a paycheck. Healthcare people cannot afford. A commute that swallows the day. I am running to change that. Not with promises, but with work. I am humbled to have her trust, and I will work every day to be worthy of it."
  },
  {
   "id": 454,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/issues/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "On the Issues - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "On the Issues - Oliver Gilbert for Congress Gas is $5 a gallon, rent is half your paycheck, and every trip to the grocery store gets more expensive. For far too many neighbors, this has been the reality for far too long. Oliver Gilbert lived these challenges growing up in Miami Gardens, working his way through college and law school, and leading our city as Mayor and County Commissioner."
  },
  {
   "id": 455,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/issues/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "On the Issues - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "What do President Trump and Washington Republicans do to help during these tough times? They spend your money on a war you didn’t ask for, didn’t vote for, and don’t need. They build a billion dollar ballroom for the Mar-a-Lago crowd. And they even use your own money to lie right to your face, spending millions on TV ads to deny the truth and divide our communities. South Florida families have had enough. It’s time to Put People First. We’re the richest country on earth, but we send billions of dollars to other countries so they can afford universal healthcare. How does that make sense? In Congress, Oliver will fight for a pathway to ensure that healthcare is a right for every American."
  },
  {
   "id": 456,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/issues/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "On the Issues - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Eliminate Income Taxes for Working Families Families who are working hard to make ends meet shouldn’t have to carry the same tax burden as billionaires. The IRS should be spending more time auditing the ultra-wealthy than scrutinizing an Uber driver’s gas deduction. Oliver supports common sense tax policies indexed to what families in our communities actually earn, so that relief reaches the people who need it most and keeps money in working people’s hands."
  },
  {
   "id": 457,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/issues/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "On the Issues - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Our government has shamefully spent billions ripping families apart. They said ICE would only target criminals, but every day more and more hardworking people are being arrested and deported, often leaving young children behind to fend for themselves or leaving the only country they’ve ever known. It’s time to end funding for these shameful deportation policies and redirect that investment where it belongs: into our communities."
  },
  {
   "id": 458,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/issues/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "On the Issues - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Countries around the world have made universal childcare a reality. As a father, Oliver knows the challenges families are facing every day. In Washington, he will redirect spending toward our children and families, so that the resources no longer being wasted on mass deportations start building something that actually lasts. In Congress, Oliver will fight to secure the federal funding needed to ensure the job gets done, and that our residents get the transit solutions they’ve been promised for decades."
  },
  {
   "id": 459,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/issues/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "On the Issues - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Oliver will fight in Washington to reinvest in job training, especially in high-paying technical fields that can’t easily be taken away by AI, and to strengthen support for entrepreneurs and small business owners. America should not only be the best place in the world to work. It should be the best place in the world to start a business. Every student deserves a pathway to purpose. The BUILD Act prepares students for the economy of tomorrow by connecting education to real careers, expanding apprenticeships, supporting teachers, rewarding innovation, and building the workforce America needs to compete."
  },
  {
   "id": 460,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/issues/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "On the Issues - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Every person with a lifelong disability deserves healthcare, a safe home, meaningful relationships, and the support to live with dignity throughout every stage of life. The HOME Act lowers monthly housing costs without weakening lending standards — helping responsible families own a home, build generational wealth, and gain long-term financial stability."
  },
  {
   "id": 461,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/about/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "My Story - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "I grew up here. I went to school here. I served here. And every step of that journey is the reason I’m running. I was raised in Miami Gardens by two people who didn’t always see the world the same way. My mom was a Seventh-day Adventist teacher. My dad was a Baptist preacher. And in our house, I learned something early: people don’t have to agree on everything to love each other, to build a life together, to raise a family together. They respected each other. They built something. That stayed with me."
  },
  {
   "id": 462,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/about/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "My Story - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Parkview Elementary. Parkway Middle. Miami Norland Senior High School. Every year of K through 12 happened right here. The teachers who taught me, the neighbors who watched me grow up, the friends who became family — they’re the reason I’m running, and they’re who I’m running for. Florida A&M was my first real test. There were nights I lived out of my car. The work ethic and faith I brought from home are the only reasons I made it through. I learned that hardship isn’t something to perform — it’s something you live through, and what you do after defines you."
  },
  {
   "id": 463,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/about/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "My Story - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Law school meant a commute. I’d ride the 27 bus all the way down 27th Avenue to the Martin Luther King Metrorail station, then take the train to Coral Gables for class at the University of Miami School of Law. Some nights I’d get back late. And my dad would meet me at the MLK station. Every time. And he’d ask me one question. He wasn’t asking for himself. He wanted the knowledge to come back home. That question shaped everything I’ve done since."
  },
  {
   "id": 464,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/about/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "My Story - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "I had the honor of serving as Mayor of my hometown for eight years. We worked on what mattered: safer neighborhoods, more parks, real economic growth, the kind of community policing that builds trust instead of breaking it. In 2020, Miami Gardens was named an All-America City — the first time in our history. I’m proud of that. But I’m more proud of what made it possible: a community that decided to invest in itself."
  },
  {
   "id": 465,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/about/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "My Story - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "On the County Commission, I’ve focused on a new goal: Make Miami-Dade County a truly world-class community. To get there, we have to overhaul our transportation system, which is why I’ve led bold initiatives to build up density along our transit corridors, creating partnerships that will fund rapid transit expansion and lead to more affordable housing in the neighborhoods that need it the most. What I’ve seen serving this community is simple. People want the same things. Good schools. Healthcare they can actually access. A commute that doesn’t take their life from them. A small business that can compete. A future their kids can build on."
  },
  {
   "id": 466,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/about/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "My Story - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "That’s what this campaign is about. Not running against anyone. Running toward something. Building a future that works for everyone, across South Florida."
  },
  {
   "id": 467,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/build-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "BUILD Act - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Every student deserves a pathway to purpose. The BUILD Act prepares students for the economy of tomorrow by connecting education to real careers, expanding apprenticeships, supporting teachers, rewarding innovation, and building the workforce America needs to compete. In-Demand Careers Stronger Workforce. Stronger America. America cannot compete in tomorrow's economy with yesterday's education system. The BUILD Act recognizes that human capacity is infrastructure. Investing in people strengthens our economy, grows small businesses, and improves national competitiveness. Skills and credentials create higher-paying career paths and increase lifetime earning potential."
  },
  {
   "id": 468,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/build-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "BUILD Act - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Expanding access to education and training opens doors for every student and every community. Nine ways the BUILD Act builds America's workforce. Tap any item to expand. Federal incentive grants reward school districts that develop career pathways in AI, cybersecurity, healthcare, advanced manufacturing, logistics, infrastructure, entrepreneurship, aerospace, and the skilled trades. Every student graduates college ready, trade ready, entrepreneurially ready, or workforce ready through certifications, dual enrollment, apprenticeships, and career pathways."
  },
  {
   "id": 469,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/build-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "BUILD Act - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Educational assistance for trade school, college, graduate school, and professional school in exchange for service in designated national priority industries. Enhanced Public Service Loan Forgiveness Expand and modernize loan forgiveness for teachers, nurses, first responders, military personnel, public defenders, and other public service professionals. Competitive federal grants reward districts that embrace innovation, workforce readiness, measurable outcomes, and industry partnerships. Enhanced grants for districts investing in teacher compensation, teacher retention, mentoring, and professional development. Teachers are America's first responders for the future."
  },
  {
   "id": 470,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/build-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "BUILD Act - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Accomplished professionals including engineers, physicians, scientists, entrepreneurs, artists, musicians, architects, attorneys, journalists, software developers, skilled trades professionals, veterans, and researchers may co-teach advanced courses for one semester. Certified teachers remain the teacher of record while BUILD Fellows contribute real-world expertise. National recognition and additional grant eligibility for school districts demonstrating exceptional workforce preparation and student success. Increase funding for Historically Black Colleges and Universities and other colleges that provide education to underserved communities. Higher wages create higher tax revenues."
  },
  {
   "id": 471,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/build-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "BUILD Act - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "More apprenticeships reduce workforce shortages. Public-private partnerships maximize taxpayer investment. Reward results instead of imposing mandates. Teachers are America's first responders for the future. Police officers respond when communities are in crisis. Firefighters respond when buildings are burning. Emergency medical personnel respond when lives are in immediate danger. Teachers respond before those crises ever occur by preparing the next generation with the knowledge, discipline, critical thinking, and character that strengthen our communities and our economy. Every student deserves a pathway to purpose."
  },
  {
   "id": 472,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/build-business-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "BUILD Business Act - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "BUILD Business Act - Oliver Gilbert for Congress America should not only be the best place in the world to work. It should be the best place in the world to start a business. Small businesses are the backbone of the American economy. The BUILD Business Act modernizes the Small Business Administration by expanding access to capital, reducing barriers to entrepreneurship, and helping more Americans start, grow, and expand successful businesses. Too many entrepreneurs have the talent and determination to succeed but cannot access the capital needed to get started. The BUILD Business Act closes that gap by pairing affordable financing with mentorship, accountability, and streamlined government."
  },
  {
   "id": 473,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/build-business-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "BUILD Business Act - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Eleven concrete actions to help Americans start, grow, and expand small businesses. Tap any item to expand. Create the American Small Business Grant Program providing grants of $5,000 to $25,000 for equipment, inventory, software, licensing, insurance, lease deposits, and other startup costs. Goal: Give entrepreneurs access to capital before debt becomes necessary. Establish the SBA Growth Line offering low interest loans, generally from 0% to 2%, with deferred repayment. Goal: Help growing businesses scale without being overwhelmed by early debt."
  },
  {
   "id": 474,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/build-business-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "BUILD Business Act - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Strengthen the SBA 7(a) program by increasing federal guarantees, reducing borrower fees, simplifying approvals, speeding processing, and expanding lending in underserved communities. Strengthen the SBA 504 program by expanding funding, modernizing eligibility, speeding project approvals, and creating a new 504 Express Expansion track for established businesses creating jobs. Provide enhanced financing incentives for businesses that establish employee ownership and profit-sharing programs. Goal: Help workers build wealth alongside the businesses they help build. Combine startup grants, affordable financing, technical assistance, and contracting opportunities in targeted commercial corridors."
  },
  {
   "id": 475,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/build-business-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "BUILD Business Act - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Goal: Revitalize communities through local entrepreneurship. Reduce lender risk by covering the initial portion of losses on qualifying startup loans. Goal: Encourage more private lending to promising entrepreneurs. Create one digital portal for grants, loans, mentoring, technical assistance, and contracting opportunities. Goal: Make government easier to navigate. Expand Mentorship and Business Development Partner with universities, chambers of commerce, Small Business Development Centers, experienced business mentors, minority business organizations, and local economic development agencies."
  },
  {
   "id": 476,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/build-business-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "BUILD Business Act - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Publish annual reports measuring business creation, job creation, survival rates, loan performance, and taxpayer return on investment. Simplify procurement and help more small businesses compete for government contracts. Goal: Create reliable customers, not just affordable financing. Reduce paperwork, simplify reporting requirements, coordinate permitting where possible, and expand digital services. Goal: Let entrepreneurs spend more time growing businesses. Opening your first restaurant? Access startup grants and affordable financing. Buying your first commercial building? A strengthened SBA 504 program makes expansion easier."
  },
  {
   "id": 477,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/build-business-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "BUILD Business Act - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Growing a construction, trucking, retail, or service business? A stronger SBA 7(a) program helps finance hiring and equipment. Veteran, first-time entrepreneur, or business owner in an underserved community? Benefit from expanded mentoring and streamlined access to capital. Employee? Expanded ownership incentives create more opportunities to build wealth. The BUILD Business Act shifts federal policy from simply recruiting employers to creating more of them. When small businesses succeed, communities create jobs, families build wealth, neighborhoods become stronger, and America's economy grows from the ground up. Improve five-year business survival rates."
  },
  {
   "id": 478,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/build-business-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "BUILD Business Act - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Expand lending in underserved communities. Grow federal contracts awarded to small businesses. Increase locally owned businesses and local job creation. Require business plans for grant applicants. Maintain prudent underwriting standards for loans. Publish annual audits and performance reports. Investigate and prosecute fraud aggressively."
  },
  {
   "id": 479,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress A Full Life. A Secure Future. A Promise That Lasts. Every person with a lifelong disability deserves healthcare, a safe home, meaningful relationships, and the support to live with dignity throughout every stage of life. For millions of families, the hardest question is not what happens today. It is what happens tomorrow."
  },
  {
   "id": 480,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Parents of children with intellectual, developmental, and other lifelong disabilities often spend decades serving as caregivers, advocates, benefits experts, transportation coordinators, housing planners, and emergency responders. They hold together a system that was never designed to work as one system. When a child becomes an adult, families can face separate rules for Medicaid, Medicare, Social Security, housing, employment services, transportation, and community programming. A parent may have to contact multiple agencies just to keep basic services in place. Then comes the question no family should have to face alone: What happens when the parent becomes sick, grows older, or dies?"
  },
  {
   "id": 481,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Too often, the answer is a crisis. Housing is disrupted. Caregivers disappear. Benefits lapse. Siblings are asked to take over without preparation. Adults who have lived in the community may face isolation or unnecessary institutional placement. That is not a system of care. It is a system of uncertainty. The CARE Act creates a comprehensive federal framework for lifelong care and community living. It brings existing programs together, fills the gaps between them, and ensures that every eligible person has one coordinated plan for life. No person should lose healthcare, housing, caregiving, or community because a parent can no longer provide care."
  },
  {
   "id": 482,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "The CARE Act is built around eight commitments . Tap any item to expand. Every eligible person will have one federally certified CARE Advocate beginning during the transition to adulthood and continuing throughout life. The CARE Advocate becomes the family's single point of contact and coordinates services across Medicaid, Medicare, Social Security, housing, healthcare, transportation, employment, education, and community programs. What it means One person responsible for making sure the whole system works together."
  },
  {
   "id": 483,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Eligible individuals will receive timely access to necessary home and community-based services, including personal assistance, nursing, therapies, behavioral healthcare, transportation, respite care, supported employment, day services, residential support, and emergency backup care. What it means Community care should be dependable, not something families wait years to receive."
  },
  {
   "id": 484,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "The CARE Act will expand accessible housing modeled after successful efforts such as Casa Familia, including supported apartments, small shared homes, mixed-income communities, independent living options, and higher-support residences. Housing funding and care funding will be coordinated instead of treated as unrelated programs. What it means The goal is not simply a bed. The goal is a home and a community."
  },
  {
   "id": 485,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Community Belonging Grants will support programs that create real relationships and full community participation. That includes models similar to Friendship Circle, Best Buddies, Special Olympics, faith-based inclusion programs, arts, recreation, volunteer service, peer mentoring, and civic engagement. What it means A full life includes friends, places to go, people who know your name, and opportunities to contribute."
  },
  {
   "id": 486,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Beginning in adolescence, each participant and family will create a Lifelong Support Plan covering housing, healthcare, communication needs, transportation, employment, daily support, emergency care, financial planning, future caregivers, and supported decision-making. The plan will follow the individual and be updated over time. What it means The transition after a parent's death should never begin with strangers trying to reconstruct a person's life. The CARE Act expands respite care, caregiver training, mental health support, sibling planning, legal and financial guidance, emergency caregiver networks, and transition assistance."
  },
  {
   "id": 487,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "What it means Parents should be allowed to be parents, not unpaid administrators of a broken system. The plan invests in direct support professionals through better reimbursement, competitive wages, training, career ladders, benefits, recruitment, retention, and emergency staffing. What it means A promise of care means little if there is no one available to provide it. The CARE Act will make assistive technology part of the basic support plan, including communication devices, smart-home systems, wearable health tools, remote monitoring chosen by the individual, adaptive robotics, mobility technology, accessible transportation, and digital care coordination."
  },
  {
   "id": 488,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "What it means Technology should increase independence and safety without replacing human connection or personal choice. The CARE Advocate is the practical center of the plan. This person will not replace a parent, guardian, caregiver, doctor, or benefits agency. The advocate will make sure they are communicating and working from one coordinated plan. Helps the individual and family create and update the Lifelong Support Plan. Coordinates applications, renewals, and transitions involving Medicaid, Medicare, Social Security, housing, employment, and transportation. Organizes annual meetings with the individual, family, caregivers, providers, and appropriate agencies."
  },
  {
   "id": 489,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Maintains an emergency and successor-care plan. Tracks deadlines and prevents avoidable gaps in benefits or services. Helps resolve disputes and escalates urgent needs when agencies fail to respond. Monitors actual quality of life, not merely whether forms were completed. Remains accountable to the individual and respects supported decision-making, privacy, choice, and independence. Federal agencies will retain their legal authority over eligibility and benefits. The CARE Advocate will have statutory coordination authority, access to participating agencies with the individual's consent, and the ability to require timely responses and elevate unresolved cases."
  },
  {
   "id": 490,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Every participant will have one secure, portable Lifelong Support Plan recognized across participating programs. The individual must be at the center of that plan, with family and trusted supporters involved according to the individual's preferences and legal rights. Communication preferences and assistive technology Education, employment, volunteering, and meaningful daytime activity Friendships, recreation, faith, culture, and community participation Supported decision-making or guardianship arrangements Social Security, representative payee, ABLE account, trust, and financial planning Successor caregivers and the transition when parents can no longer provide care"
  },
  {
   "id": 491,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "The CARE Act will establish continuous coverage and coordinated care for people with qualifying lifelong disabilities. Medicaid will remain the principal payer for long-term services and supports. Medicare will cover eligible medical services. Social Security will provide income support. The CARE Advocate will make those systems function as one plan instead of separate bureaucracies. Prevent unnecessary interruptions in Medicaid for people with permanent qualifying disabilities. Provide Medicaid wraparound coverage for services Medicare does not cover. Expand access to Medicaid Buy-In so people can work without losing essential care."
  },
  {
   "id": 492,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Require coverage of emergency backup caregiving and transition support. Reduce repetitive paperwork and duplicative disability reviews where the condition is permanent. Protect continuity when an individual moves between communities or across state lines. 06 / Building More Places Like Casa Familia The CARE Act will create a national Community Living Capital Fund to help nonprofit organizations, local governments, housing providers, and families build or preserve accessible community housing. The program will coordinate HUD housing resources, federal tax incentives, local land, nonprofit investment, and Medicaid-funded services."
  },
  {
   "id": 493,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Federal support should be flexible enough to help create different options because adults with disabilities do not all need or want the same living arrangement. Small homes shared by a limited number of residents Supported apartments with staff available on site Mixed-income and mixed-ability developments Independent apartments with visiting support Residences designed for people with more significant medical or behavioral needs The standard must be dignity, safety, individual choice, and meaningful connection to the surrounding community. Community living cannot become institutional care with a nicer sign out front."
  },
  {
   "id": 494,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "One coordinated promise replaces a patchwork of disconnected programs. Here is the difference for families living it every day. One CARE Advocate coordinates the entire plan. Community services can depend on a waiting list. Necessary lifelong supports are guaranteed on a timely basis. Succession and emergency planning begin during adolescence. Housing, services, transportation, and community programming are coordinated. Parents worry about what happens when they die. A successor-care plan, stable housing, and a support team are already in place. Success is measured by safety, health, independence, relationships, purpose, and belonging. 08 / How the Federal Government Will Work Together"
  },
  {
   "id": 495,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "The CARE Act does not pretend that one existing agency can do everything. It gives each agency a clear responsibility and creates one coordinated system around the individual. Oversees the CARE Advocate Corps, national standards, community inclusion grants, family support, and quality-of-life accountability. Funds long-term services and supports, personal care, residential services, therapies, respite, transportation, and care coordination. Supports accessible housing construction, rental assistance, nonprofit development, and community living options. Administers SSI, Disabled Adult Child benefits, income support, and representative payee services."
  },
  {
   "id": 496,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Provides medical coverage for eligible participants, coordinated with Medicaid wraparound services. Support transition, workforce preparation, supported employment, and opportunities to contribute. Expands accessible and dependable transportation and future mobility solutions. States, Counties, and Community Partners Deliver services locally and develop housing, programs, and care networks tailored to their communities. 09 / Protecting Choice and Preventing Abuse"
  },
  {
   "id": 497,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "A stronger care system must also protect the rights of the people it serves. The CARE Act will include independent oversight, transparent reporting, background and training standards, accessible complaint procedures, protection against abuse and financial exploitation, and regular review of restrictive guardianships. No housing provider, caregiver, guardian, or government agency should control a person's life simply because that person needs support. The individual's voice, preferences, safety, and right to live in the community must remain at the center of every decision."
  },
  {
   "id": 498,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "The federal government will be required to report whether participants are actually living better lives. Measures will include: Continuity of healthcare and support services Preventable hospitalizations and emergency placements Employment, education, volunteering, or meaningful daily activity Personal choice and supported decision-making Caregiver stability and workforce retention Avoidance of unnecessary institutionalization Perfect paperwork and an isolated life is not success. A parent's death will always be a profound personal loss. It should not also become a housing crisis, a healthcare crisis, and a caregiving crisis."
  },
  {
   "id": 499,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "The CARE Act will help adults build stable lives, homes, relationships, routines, and support networks while their parents are still alive. It will make sure the people who know and care for them are not replaced by a frantic search for services after a crisis. Independence does not mean facing life alone. It means having the support to live the fullest life possible. No. A CARE Advocate coordinates programs and protects continuity. The advocate does not automatically control legal, medical, or financial decisions. Supported decision-making and the individual's own choices remain central. Would this replace Medicaid or Social Security?"
  },
  {
   "id": 500,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "No. It would make those programs work together. Medicaid would generally fund long-term care and community supports. Social Security would provide income support. HUD would support housing, and Medicare would continue covering eligible medical care. Would every person have to live in a specialized disability community? No. The plan expands choices. Some people may prefer an independent apartment, a mixed community, a small shared home, a residence near family, or a community designed around specialized support. The individual's needs and preferences should guide the decision. What happens while parents are still alive?"
  },
  {
   "id": 501,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "Planning and transition begin early. The adult develops relationships with caregivers, the CARE Advocate, community programs, and future supporters before a crisis occurs. Parents remain partners, but they are no longer the entire system. The CARE Act coordinates existing federal programs and adds targeted investments in community care, housing, the caregiving workforce, technology, and family support. Preventing avoidable hospitalizations, homelessness, emergency placements, and unnecessary institutional care can also reduce costly crises."
  },
  {
   "id": 502,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl24-gilbert",
   "url": "https://olivergilbert.vote/care-act/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "CARE Act - Lifelong Care and Community for Americans with Disabilities - Oliver Gilbert for Congress",
   "text": "The legislation will establish functional and clinical eligibility for individuals with significant lifelong intellectual, developmental, and other disabilities who require ongoing support. Eligibility must be clear, fair, and portable across states. Families should not have to spend a lifetime worrying about what happens next. The CARE Act creates a clear promise of lifelong care, housing, healthcare, dignity, and belonging."
  },
  {
   "id": 503,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "Miami Beach Born, Lauderdale Raised, Boca Raton Mayor Scott Singer is the Republican nominee running to represent Florida’s 25th district in Congress, the district where he was born and raised and has lived for 40 years. As Congressman, he will keep taxes and costs low, ensure strong borders and national defense, and cut waste, fraud, and abuse. He will work with President Trump and colleagues in Congress to advance common-sense solutions to improve our economy and protect our nation."
  },
  {
   "id": 504,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "Scott has a strong record of results as the three-term Mayor of Boca Raton where he balanced budgets while working to advance public safety, education, affordability, and accountability. Scott voted seven straight times to lower the tax rate to ensure Boca Raton has the lowest property tax of any full-service city in Florida. He was a political outsider who shook up City Hall and will fight for the interests of our residents against Washington insiders and career politicians."
  },
  {
   "id": 505,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "As Mayor, Scott led innovative efforts to partner for more classroom seats, improved school safety, and mobility solutions, while increasing accountability by streamlining and cutting red tape. Scott attracted strategic investment to add high paying jobs while cutting government costs to help affordability. He streamlined and cut red tape, while investing to ensure public safety and infrastructure are priorities."
  },
  {
   "id": 506,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "Now, Scott is running for Congress to deliver common-sense, America First policies that protect our families, our safety, and our future. He supports a term limits amendment, pledged not to raise taxes, and will vote to ban members of Congress from trading stocks. He will defend the U.S. Constitution and ensure unelected bureaucrats will not be able to impose their agendas on the American people. Scott will stand up to a radical far-left agenda that weakens our nation and threatens our important relationships with allies like Israel."
  },
  {
   "id": 507,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "Scott was born and first lived in Miami Beach before growing up in Fort Lauderdale. Having lived on the barrier islands for more than 20 years and in an apartment on A1A, Scott knows the issues facing condo residents like assessments, beachside concerns, and mobility. He graduated from Pine Crest School, Harvard University, and Georgetown Law.  A small business owner, Scott has worked for two decades as a lawyer to also help businesses and entrepreneurs add jobs and overcome burdensome and wasteful regulations that raise costs."
  },
  {
   "id": 508,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "As the inaugural Chair of the America First Policy Institute Mayors’ Council, Scott leads a national group of mayors working to advance America First solutions and improve our cities. Singer has been active in a variety of nonprofit and leadership roles and has earned broad bipartisan support throughout his service. Scott has been a strong voice against antisemitism, and an advocate for stronger national security that safeguards our borders and protects our future. Scott’s family fled communism and he will stand up to far-left proposals to abolish prisons and federal law enforcement or private health care."
  },
  {
   "id": 509,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "Scott and his wife, Bella, are the proud parents of two children, and Scott is motivated to work for the next generation to ensure a better future for our community, our state, and our nation. Terms & Conditions + Privacy Policy apply. Jobs & Economy - A Proven Record of Strong Results Respect the Rule of Law & Stand with Law Enforcement Committed to a Strong National Defense and Military Scott Pledged to Keep Taxes Low and Has Delivered Advance Free-Market Capitalism & Oppose Socialism Cryptocurrency and Digital Asset Innovation Increasing Accountability and Transparency History of Service & Community Involvement Standing with Israel & our Jewish Community"
  },
  {
   "id": 510,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/priorities",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Scott's Priorities | Join the Movement for Prosperity — SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "Scott's Priorities | Join the Movement for Prosperity — SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS Jobs & Economy - A Proven Record of Strong Results Like President Trump, Scott understands what it takes to manage a successful business. Additionally, as mayor, he worked to support local businesses by reducing red tape, increasing the use of technology, and adding more high-paying jobs to our thriving economy. As our next congressman, Scott will work hand in hand with our local business leaders to build consensus on plans for sustained long-term financial growth for our South Florida communities."
  },
  {
   "id": 511,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/priorities",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Scott's Priorities | Join the Movement for Prosperity — SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "Scott supports the Administration's work to slash overregulation that burdens businesses and raises costs for consumers. As mayor, he advanced many streamlining initiatives to cut red tape and bureaucracy, increased technology use, and attracted businesses to bring high-paying jobs for residents. When in Congress, Scott will work to put into law the many gains from the Trump executive orders that are unleashing our economy so that our families have more opportunity and greater affordability. Scott supports energy independence to advance our economy free from destabilizing foreign influences and to reduce costs for our nation. Respect the Rule of Law & Stand with Law Enforcement"
  },
  {
   "id": 512,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/priorities",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Scott's Priorities | Join the Movement for Prosperity — SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "As mayor, Scott has consistently increased investment to ensure the best in public safety. While other cities defunded police and refused to prosecute, Boca Raton continued to have one of the highest starting salaries for police officers in the nation to attract and retain the best professionals to keep our neighborhoods safe. Scott strongly supports President Trump’s efforts to secure the border and turn back the failed Biden policies that allowed millions of people into our nation outside of the normal vetting process. Singer knows that a secure border is reducing the crises from fentanyl and opioids that are ravaging communities and tearing apart families."
  },
  {
   "id": 513,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/priorities",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Scott's Priorities | Join the Movement for Prosperity — SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "Scott stands with our local law enforcement officers who have come under baseless attacks by the radical left in recent years. He knows that public safety is the first function of government and deserves our strong support. As a father of two young children, Scott will keep making sure our neighborhoods and homes are safe. He also wants to make sure our children are safe in cyberspace. Scott has worked to ensure our police and fire rescue services attract and retain the best talent and have the necessary tools and resources to serve and protect our citizens. Committed to a Strong Military and Defense"
  },
  {
   "id": 514,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/priorities",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Scott's Priorities | Join the Movement for Prosperity — SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "As mayor, Scott ensured that funding went to public safety, not woke or race-based programs. As congressman, he will ensure that our brave military men and women receive the support and training they need so that America is prepared for any threat. Scott will always advocate for policies that protect our military warfighters from being put into harm’s way and our nation’s collective national defense. Scott stands with our veterans and will work to ensure that we take care of our brave patriots at all stages of their lives. Scott Pledged to Keep Taxes Low and Has Delivered"
  },
  {
   "id": 515,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/priorities",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Scott's Priorities | Join the Movement for Prosperity — SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "Scott’s core principles have always centered around keeping taxes low so that more money was in the pockets of American families. Scott has voted for multiple years in a row to lower the property tax rate, never voted for a tax-rate increase, and ensured Boca Raton has the lowest property tax rate of any full-service city in Florida. At the same time, Boca Raton has invested in infrastructure to keep other costs like water rates far cheaper than other cities."
  },
  {
   "id": 516,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/priorities",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Scott's Priorities | Join the Movement for Prosperity — SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "Scott stands with President Trump on his work to provide the largest tax cut in American history and will oppose efforts to increase tax rates. In Congress, Scott will work to continue cuts of the incredibly wasteful spending like billions lost in the Biden years spent overseas on ridiculous programs. Fiscal discipline for America First means spending wisely to take care of our core needs so families keep more of their own money. Advance Free-Market Capitalism & Oppose Socialism Scott Singer will work to help advance the America First agenda by sponsoring bills to make permanent President Trump's policies that are unleashing our economy and moving America forward."
  },
  {
   "id": 517,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/priorities",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Scott's Priorities | Join the Movement for Prosperity — SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "Scott is a staunch supporter of President Donald J. Trump's leadership to cut waste and fraud from the budget. In Congress, he will work to help advance the America First agenda by sponsoring laws to make permanent the policies that are unleashing our economy and moving America forward. Scott strongly supports the President’s strong response to threats from China, Russia, and Iran that have brought peace through strength here and across the globe. Scott has worked to advance skilled trades and manufacturing jobs to provide pathways to prosperity for millions of American and increase jobs. The America First economic and trade policy will restore the American Dream for generations."
  },
  {
   "id": 518,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/priorities",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Scott's Priorities | Join the Movement for Prosperity — SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "Scott believes America is the greatest country in the world and will oppose all actions of the radical left to institute debilitating socialist policies here at home. Standing with Israel & our Jewish Community Israel has had no greater friend than President Trump, and as congressman, Scott will work with the president to continue to stand with America’s strongest ally in the region and President Trump's bold efforts to prevent a nuclear Iran. Scott will advocate a strong national defense by ensuring we support our allies and stop threats that look to destabilize the West."
  },
  {
   "id": 519,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/priorities",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Scott's Priorities | Join the Movement for Prosperity — SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "At home, Scott worked to ensure safety for our houses of worship and Jewish day schools and will fight to expand existing federal funding for nonprofits at risk of terrorist or extremist attacks. He will continue to stand strong against antisemitism amid the increased bigotry from the extremes and will call it out, unlike Democrats who had two dozen members of Congress shamefully portray Israel’s response to brutal attacks on civilians as genocide. Harmful rhetoric makes our community less safe. Cryptocurrency and Digital Asset Innovation"
  },
  {
   "id": 520,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/priorities",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Scott's Priorities | Join the Movement for Prosperity — SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "Scott supports the ability of cryptocurrency to give individuals more control and transparency for how they want to store their money. Scott will defend your wallet, your safety, and your freedoms. Increasing Accountability and Transparency As mayor, he has also championed reforms to increase accountability, ethics standards, and transparency in local government. As congressman, he will vote to prohibit members of Congress from stock trading. Scott supports banning American schools and universities who receive foreign funding for programming from receiving federal dollars. Defending Our Communities and Constitutional Rights"
  },
  {
   "id": 521,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/priorities",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Scott's Priorities | Join the Movement for Prosperity — SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "Scott has always stood with our brave law enforcement officers, funding to ensure the best police professionals, leading to a 25% drop in crime rates when he was mayor – from what were already 40-year lows. Scott stood up to challenge a law that could have had police officers responsible to pay for their own defense even when acting lawfully. At the same time, Scott will protect our Second Amendment rights against attempts to infringe on them. He knows that lawful gun owners deserve our rights and that we need to focus on stopping criminals, greater enforcement of existing laws, and more mental health treatment."
  },
  {
   "id": 522,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl25-singer",
   "url": "https://www.scottsingerusa.com/priorities",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Scott's Priorities | Join the Movement for Prosperity — SCOTT SINGER FOR CONGRESS",
   "text": "Scott knows this district as a lifelong resident and as a mayor and the need for coordinated transportation planning along our nearly 30 communities. He will work for better federal solutions for our roadways, bridges, and coastline – something many residents feel was neglected by prior representatives. He will push to streamline the federal permitting process as he did many times as mayor, leading to savings of tax dollars and time. Scott will push for greater action by Congress to expand insurance programs that will save our taxpayers more of their dollars. This coastal district has unique needs for flooding and windstorms, and Scott will work to increase federal support to lower costs."
  },
