   "kind": "official_issues",
   "title": "Transportation and Housing | Congressman Mario Diaz-Balart",
   "text": "WASHINGTON, D.C. – Congressman Mario Díaz-Balart (FL-26), Vice Chair of the House Appropriations Committee, issued the following statement after the House Appropriations Committee approved the Congressman Mario Díaz-Balart Delivers $2M in Funding for Feasibility Analysis for Proposed Interchange at I-75 and Everglades Boulevard Project NAPLES, FL - Congressman Mario Díaz-Balart (FL-26), Vice Chair of the House Appropriations Committee and Dean of the Florida Congressional Delegation, presented $2,000,000 in federal funding to Collier County for a feasibility analysis to open the Everglades Boulevard interchange location on a portion of I-75."
  },
  {
   "id": 617,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl26-diaz-balart",
   "url": "https://mariodiazbalart.house.gov/issues/transportation-and-housing",
   "kind": "official_issues",
   "title": "Transportation and Housing | Congressman Mario Diaz-Balart",
   "text": "Residents of eastern Collier County lack a southern interchange that provides direct access to the interstate. MEDIA ADVISORY: Rep. Díaz-Balart to Deliver $2M for the Feasibility Analysis for Proposed Interchange at I-75 and Everglades Boulevard Project NAPLES, FL –  Representative Mario Díaz-Balart (FL-26) is pleased to invite members of the media to attend a special check presentation ceremony on Monday, May 11th, at 11 a.m."
  },
  {
   "id": 618,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl26-diaz-balart",
   "url": "https://mariodiazbalart.house.gov/issues/transportation-and-housing",
   "kind": "official_issues",
   "title": "Transportation and Housing | Congressman Mario Diaz-Balart",
   "text": "The event celebrates the $2 million in funding secured for the feasibility analysis for the proposed interchange at I-75 and the Everglades Boulevard Project. This project would be used to assess the possibility of opening the existing Everglades Boulevard interchange located on a portion of I-75. Congressman Mario Diaz-Balart Delivers Nearly $5 Million in Federal Funds to Combat Flooding and Improve Safety in Hialeah HIALEAH, FL - Congressman Mario Díaz-Balart (FL-26), Vice Chair of the House Appropriations Committee and Dean of the Florida Congressional Delegation, presented $4,900,000 in federal funding to the City of Hialeah for stormwater improvements in Southeast Hialeah."
  },
  {
