   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Rep. Carlos Gimenez Secures Major Wins for South Florida | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "$593,600 for Miami for the Water Pollution Prevention Project: This funding will be used to prevent pollution from Goulds canal to L-31E canal and the area of the CERP Biscayne Bay Coastal Wetlands’ S-705 pump station by backfilling a section of Goulds canal from L-31E Canal to the eastern end of Goulds canal."
  },
  {
   "id": 964,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2024/3/rep-carlos-gimenez-secures-major-wins-for-florida-s-28th-district",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Rep. Carlos Gimenez Secures Major Wins for South Florida | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Congressman Carlos Gim&eacute;nez represents Miami-Dade County and the beautiful Florida Keys. He is the only Cuban-born Member of the 118th Congress, having fled his homeland shortly after the Communist takeover of the island. He is the first career firefighter paramedic elected to the House of Representatives and served as the former Fire Chief of the City of Miami and Mayor of Miami-Dade County. He serves on the House Armed Services Committee, the Homeland Security Committee, and the Select Committee on China. Permalink: https://gimenez.house.gov/2024/3/rep-carlos-gimenez-secures-major-wins-for-florida-s-28th-district"
  },
  {
   "id": 965,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/2/enough-is-enough-it-s-time-to-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Enough is enough—it’s time to act | Newsletters | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Enough is enough—it’s time to act | Newsletters | Congressman Carlos Gimenez Resources for American Citizens in Israel The crisis at our borders is spiraling out of control, and now, Florida is facing an unprecedented wave of illegal migration from Communist China. We’ve seen an 8,000% increase in the number of migrants from Communist China flooding into Miami and the Keys from the Bahamas and the Caribbean. This is a direct threat to our national security, and we must act now! As security at the southern border tightens, smugglers are finding alternative routes and our district, Miami and the Florida Keys, is paying the price."
  },
  {
   "id": 966,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/2/enough-is-enough-it-s-time-to-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Enough is enough—it’s time to act | Newsletters | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "The Bahamas must work to end the illegal migrants flooding the island and our communities. We cannot allow our adversaries to exploit weak enforcement and put American lives at risk. I will continue fighting to close loopholes, strengthen enforcement, and hold those responsible accountable. Florida will not be a gateway for illegal immigration! Congressman Carlos Gimenez Remembers Frank Toppino"
  },
  {
   "id": 967,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/2/enough-is-enough-it-s-time-to-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Enough is enough—it’s time to act | Newsletters | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "I took to the House Floor to remember Mr. Frank Toppino, World War II veteran and pillar of the Key West community. Mr. Frank’s acts of service are a true testament to his character. Let us remember his legacy of life-long dedication to family and community. Mr. Frank will be deeply missed. But his lessons will serve as an example to us all. U.S. House Passes the Protecting American Energy Production Act"
  },
  {
   "id": 968,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/2/enough-is-enough-it-s-time-to-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Enough is enough—it’s time to act | Newsletters | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "This week, the House of Representatives passed the Protecting American Energy Production Act which will lower prices and jumpstart energy production here in the US. America must become energy independent while also rejecting and putting an end to the socialist Green New Deal. I urge my Senate colleagues to pass this vital legislation. Congressman Carlos Gimenez Welcomes the Columbus Explorers I am always honored to speak to my fellow Columbus Explorers. These men are the next leaders of Miami and this great nation. Adelante and C Pride! Congressman Carlos Gimenez Welcomes City of Miami Springs Officials"
  },
  {
   "id": 969,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/2/enough-is-enough-it-s-time-to-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Enough is enough—it’s time to act | Newsletters | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "It is always great to see friends from home! It was great to welcome the City of Miami Spring’s to Washington to discuss pressing issues of the community. Congressman Carlos Gimenez Congratulates Lt. Gov. Nunez Congratulations to Florida Lt. Governor Jeanette Nunez on being chosen to lead Florida International University as its interim president. I look forward to continuing our work together to secure investments for FIU so we can continue to take the university to even greater heights. Congressman Carlos Gimenez Congratulate Amanda Fernandez"
  },
  {
   "id": 970,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/2/enough-is-enough-it-s-time-to-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Enough is enough—it’s time to act | Newsletters | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Lourdes and I were honored to congratulate Amanda Fernadez, the new President of the Cuban-American Bar Association, alongside our dear friend, State Attorney Katherine Fernandez-Rundle! Our Cuban-American Community has contributed immensely to this truly exceptional nation, and we are forever grateful to the United States of America. Thank you, Governor Desantis, for working to provide much needed relief for Florida homeowners, especially those of us in Miami and the Florida Keys as we face some of the highest rates in the nation. Congressman Carlos Gimenez Joins Fox News"
  },
  {
   "id": 971,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/2/enough-is-enough-it-s-time-to-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Enough is enough—it’s time to act | Newsletters | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "I joined Fox News to discuss the ongoing drug crisis that is directly tied to terrorist cartel organizations. This must stop now. Congressman Carlos Gimenez Joins Fox Business I joined Varney & Co. to discuss Secretary of State Rubio’s success in Panama and how he is implementing President Trump’s peace through strength throughout the world. Congressman Carlos Gimenez joined the House Natural Resources Committee as they considered his bill to integrate Osceola Camp into the Miccosukee Reserved Area. The bill was advanced out of the Subcommittee on Indian and Insular Affairs and now heads to the full committee."
  },
  {
   "id": 972,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/2/enough-is-enough-it-s-time-to-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Enough is enough—it’s time to act | Newsletters | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Congressman Carlos Gimenez was appointed by Speaker Mike Johnson to the Select Committee on the Chinese Communist Party . H.R. 26: Protecting American Energy Production Act . Passed, 226-188 (Yea). H. Res. 93: Providing for consideration of the bill (H.R. 27) to amend the Controlled Substances Act with respect to the scheduling of fentanyl-related substances, and for other purposes. Passed, 215-208 (Yea). H.R. 776: Nutria Eradication and Control Reauthorization Act of 2025 . Passed, 361-56 (Yea). H.R. 43: Alaska Native Village Municipal Lands Restoration Act of 2025. Passed, 412-1 (Yea)."
  },
  {
   "id": 973,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-gimenez",
   "url": "https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/2/enough-is-enough-it-s-time-to-act",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Enough is enough—it’s time to act | Newsletters | Congressman Carlos Gimenez",
   "text": "Need help with a passport, visa, veterans benefits, IRS, immigration or any other issue with a federal agency? Join my team, Thursday, February 13, 2025, for mobile office hours in the Key Largo - The College of the FL Keys Upper Keys - 106040 Overseas Highway, Key Largo, FL, 33037. WHERE: The College of the FL Keys Upper Keys - 106040 Overseas Highway, Key Largo, FL, 33037. If you have any questions or concerns, please contact my office at 305-222-0160 or click HERE . Permalink: https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/2/enough-is-enough-it-s-time-to-act"
  },
  {
   "id": 974,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-ehr",
   "url": "https://ehrforcongress.us/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Vote Phil Ehr for U.S. House of Representatives",
   "text": "Vote Phil Ehr for U.S. House of Representatives Phil Ehr’s first mission in the Navy was the Mariel Boatlift, where he helped rescue Cuban exiles who risked it all for freedom and opportunity in America. He went on to serve a full career in the Navy and beyond—often in harm’s way— fighting communists, fascists and terrorists. Phil’s lifelong commitment to our freedoms, democracy and prosperity continues in his campaign to replace Rep. Carlos Gimenez in Congress. Florida’s 28th Congressional District includes Southwest Miami-Dade County (West Kendall, The Hammocks, West Richmond Heights, Goulds, South Dade, Homestead, Florida City) and the beautiful Florida Keys."
  },
  {
   "id": 975,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-ehr",
   "url": "https://ehrforcongress.us/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Vote Phil Ehr for U.S. House of Representatives",
   "text": "Lower premiums, expand access, and reduce out-of-pocket costs through the Healthcare Stability & Program Choice Act. Enforce anti-fraud laws, hold bad actors accountable, stabilize the market, and protect homeowners from rising costs. Putting America First means defending the Constitution and the rule of law, rejecting anti-American rhetoric, antisemitism, socialism and political extremism, and using military force only when lawful and necessary. Create an inter-agency public corruption task force and strengthen accountability for public contracts."
  },
  {
   "id": 976,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-ehr",
   "url": "https://ehrforcongress.us/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Vote Phil Ehr for U.S. House of Representatives",
   "text": "Pursue a full VA hospital or major VA medical facility in South Dade to improve access for veterans in South Dade and Monroe County while strengthening essential services. Protect law-abiding immigrant families, Improve training and accountability for border personnel, a path to permanent residency for families stuck in legal limbo and target criminals and traffickers. Protect the Everglades, defend water resources, support responsible growth, and pursue a temporary moratorium on large-scale AI data centers and other high-impact developments until their impacts on infrastructure, energy, housing, and the environment are fully evaluated."
  },
  {
   "id": 977,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-ehr",
   "url": "https://ehrforcongress.us/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Vote Phil Ehr for U.S. House of Representatives",
   "text": "I am proud to endorse retired Navy Commander Phil Ehr for Congress. Phil Ehr has a proven track record of fighting for freedom abroad and he will fight for freedom here at home. With the House of Representatives being pushed to extremism we need candidates like Phil Ehr who will always put people before political partisanship. – Former U.S. Rep. Debbie Mucarsel-Powell Leaders like Phil Ehr exemplify unwavering integrity, relentless problem-solving, and the ability to forge new paths. Phil’s distinguished record in the Navy and beyond is a testament to these qualities."
  },
  {
   "id": 978,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-ehr",
   "url": "https://ehrforcongress.us/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Vote Phil Ehr for U.S. House of Representatives",
   "text": "The dire need for change in South Florida is clear. Our community is plagued by corruption, while Tallahassee is preoccupied with divisive culture wars, and Washington is compromised by anti-democratic extremists. Tragically, Carlos Gimenez is complicit in these grave threats. We can trust Phil Ehr to continue serving with integrity. He will find solutions that matter to everyday people in South Florida, and he’ll fight for our freedom, democracy, and prosperity. Phil Ehr is running to lower healthcare costs, fight public corruption and deliver for the families Carlos Gimenez has left behind. Help us defeat Gimenez and bring accountable leadership back to South Florida.!"
  },
  {
   "id": 979,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-ehr",
   "url": "https://ehrforcongress.us/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Vote Phil Ehr for U.S. House of Representatives",
   "text": "Phil is running for the U.S. House to continue his commitment to defending our nation and building a better future for all Floridians. Help us build a strong campaign to defeat Carlos Gimenez by making a contribution today!"
  },
  {
   "id": 980,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-ehr",
   "url": "https://ehrforcongress.us/meet-phil/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Meet Phil - Vote Phil Ehr",
   "text": "Phil Ehr advanced from Navy Seaman to Commander in a 26-year active duty career. He flew reconnaissance in the Cold War, combat support in Desert Storm, and oversaw U.S. combat operations in Allied Force, which was the most intense and sustained combat operation in Europe between World War II and Russia’s invasion of Ukraine. On shore duty, Phil provided strategic advice to senior leaders in Washington, Silicon Valley, London, and NATO, including the Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, General Colin Powell; and helped civilian agencies use declassified space technology to improve border security, federal firefighting, and earth science research."
  },
  {
   "id": 981,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-ehr",
   "url": "https://ehrforcongress.us/meet-phil/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Meet Phil - Vote Phil Ehr",
   "text": "Phil’s first mission in the Navy was the Mariel Boatlift in the Florida Strait rescuing men, women and children who risked their lives escaping brutality in Cuba for freedom and opportunity in America."
  },
  {
   "id": 982,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-ehr",
   "url": "https://ehrforcongress.us/meet-phil/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Meet Phil - Vote Phil Ehr",
   "text": "After the Navy, Phil taught children the game of chess in schools and fought Russian corruption in the World Chess Federation. Phil also taught British officers in their war college, challenged craven politicians who manipulated Americans with bigotry and lies, and founded a nonprofit to counter disinformation in domestic politics with combat-proven military tactics. Phil recently completed dozens of humanitarian aid delivery missions in Ukraine for people who—like the Cuban exiles he saw four decades earlier—risked it all for freedom."
  },
  {
   "id": 983,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-ehr",
   "url": "https://ehrforcongress.us/meet-phil/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Meet Phil - Vote Phil Ehr",
   "text": "Phil and Sue, his wife of 28 years, are blessed with two daughters. Phil is running to represent the people of South Miami-Dade and the Florida Keys, because they are suffering from extremism and chaos in Congress. New leadership is needed to solve problems that matter and to defend American freedoms, democracy and prosperity. To view Phil’s LinkedIn profile CLICK HERE . Lower premiums, expand access, and reduce out-of-pocket costs through the Healthcare Stability & Program Choice Act. Enforce anti-fraud laws, hold bad actors accountable, stabilize the market, and protect homeowners from rising costs."
  },
  {
   "id": 984,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-ehr",
   "url": "https://ehrforcongress.us/meet-phil/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Meet Phil - Vote Phil Ehr",
   "text": "Putting America First means defending the Constitution and the rule of law, rejecting anti-American rhetoric, antisemitism, socialism and political extremism, and using military force only when lawful and necessary. Create an inter-agency public corruption task force and strengthen accountability for public contracts. Pursue a full VA hospital or major VA medical facility in South Dade to improve access for veterans in South Dade and Monroe County while strengthening essential services. Protect law-abiding immigrant families, Improve training and accountability for border personnel, a path to permanent residency for families stuck in legal limbo and target criminals and traffickers."
  },
  {
   "id": 985,
   "candidate_id": "us-house-fl28-ehr",
   "url": "https://ehrforcongress.us/meet-phil/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Meet Phil - Vote Phil Ehr",
   "text": "Protect the Everglades, defend water resources, support responsible growth, and pursue a temporary moratorium on large-scale AI data centers and other high-impact developments until their impacts on infrastructure, energy, housing, and the environment are fully evaluated. We swore oaths to support and defend the Constitution because we love our families, study history and respect our varied faiths. Upholding freedoms to worship, speak and vote as we choose is the only way to preserve American ideals and achieve a brighter, friendlier Florida. May God bless America."
  },
