  {
   "id": 1080,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/about/",
   "kind": "official_home",
   "title": "About - Senator Moody",
   "text": "Senator Ashley Moody was sworn into the United States Senate on January 21, 2025, after being appointed by Governor Ron DeSantis. Ashley Moody is a fifth-generation Floridian, born and raised in Plant City, Florida. She attended the University of Florida, where she earned both her bachelor’s and master’s degrees in accounting, as well as her law degree. Additionally, she obtained a Master of Laws in International Law from Stetson University College of Law."
  },
  {
   "id": 1081,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/about/",
   "kind": "official_home",
   "title": "About - Senator Moody",
   "text": "Senator Moody began her career at the law firm Holland & Knight, where she practiced commercial litigation. In her spare time, she volunteered to assist domestic violence victims seeking protection in court. She later joined the United States Attorney’s Office, where she prosecuted drug, firearm, and fraud offenses. In 2006, at the age of thirty-one, Senator Moody became the youngest judge in Florida when she was elected as Circuit Court Judge of the Thirteenth Judicial Circuit in Hillsborough County."
  },
  {
   "id": 1082,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/about/",
   "kind": "official_home",
   "title": "About - Senator Moody",
   "text": "From 2019 to 2025, Senator Moody served as Florida’s 38th Attorney General. During her tenure, she was recognized as a national leader and served as a Commissioner on the Presidential Commission on Law Enforcement and the Administration of Justice during the first Trump administration."
  },
  {
   "id": 1083,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/about/",
   "kind": "official_home",
   "title": "About - Senator Moody",
   "text": "She also chaired Florida’s Statewide Council on Human Trafficking, led efforts against the harmful open-border policies of the Biden administration, supported and recruited law enforcement officers to protect Floridians, worked to defend children against invasive and addictive Big Tech policies, fought Big Pharma and was awarded billions of dollars for Florida through historic opioid litigation and protected Florida consumers against deceptive trade practices. As a United States Senator, Moody is focused on supporting President Trump’s agenda, securing the border, standing up for the rule of law, and continuing her work to ensure that Florida remains safe and prosperous for years to come."
  },
  {
   "id": 1084,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/about/",
   "kind": "official_home",
   "title": "About - Senator Moody",
   "text": "Senator Moody and her husband, Justin, a career law enforcement officer, have two sons, Brandon and Connor. The Committee was established in 1816 as one of the original standing committees in the United States Senate. Its broad legislative jurisdiction has assured its primary role as a forum for the public discussion of social and constitutional issues. The Committee is also responsible for oversight of key activities of the executive branch, and is responsible for the initial stages of the confirmation process of all judicial nominations for the federal judiciary. Homeland Security and Governmental Affairs Committee"
  },
  {
   "id": 1085,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/about/",
   "kind": "official_home",
   "title": "About - Senator Moody",
   "text": "The Committee on Homeland Security and Governmental Affairs (HSGAC) is the Senate’s primary oversight committee with broad jurisdiction over government operations generally and the Department of Homeland Security in particular. HELP Committee (Senate Health, Education, Labor, and Pensions Committee) Oversees legislation and issues related to health care, education, employment, pensions, A bipartisan, bicameral committee that analyzes the U.S. economy and advises Congress on economic policy. Investigates and addresses issues affecting older Americans, including retirement security, Medicare, Social Security, and elder abuse."
  },
  {
   "id": 1086,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/storm-preparation/",
   "kind": "official_issues",
   "title": "Storm Preparation - Senator Moody",
   "text": "As a fifth-generation Floridian, I have heard countless heartbreaking stories and witnessed firsthand the devastating destruction caused by hurricanes hitting our state — that is why it is crucial to be prepared. Florida has the best emergency management response in the country, but it is important to remember that while officials are working around the clock, you are the first line of defense. Make sure that you have the necessary supplies, get a plan in place, and listen to local emergency guidance. By preparing early, we can weather any storm."
  },
  {
   "id": 1087,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/storm-preparation/",
   "kind": "official_issues",
   "title": "Storm Preparation - Senator Moody",
   "text": "For additional tips on hurricane preparedness, please review the information provided by the Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA) and the Florida Division of Emergency Management (FDEM) here: https://www.ready.gov/hurricanes   (FEMA) https://www.floridadisaster.org/planprepare/   (FDEM) For weather updates, please visit the National Hurricane Center’s webpage here:   https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/ To report price gouging during a declared state of emergency, please contact the Office of the Florida Attorney General here: https://www.myfloridalegal.com/how-to-contact-us/file-a-complaint"
  },
  {
   "id": 1088,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/storm-preparation/",
   "kind": "official_issues",
   "title": "Storm Preparation - Senator Moody",
   "text": "Recovering from a storm can be an overwhelming process, especially when you have suffered loss or damage. It is vital that you understand what resources are available. Below, you will find contact information for various federal agencies that may be able to provide assistance depending on your circumstances. When you apply for aid, have the following information on hand: ·    The address of your damaged home or apartment ·    Names of people living in your household ·    A description of your disaster damages ·    A telephone number where you can be reached or left a message ·    If you want your disaster assistance funds sent directly to your bank, provide FEMA your bank information"
  },
  {
   "id": 1089,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/storm-preparation/",
   "kind": "official_issues",
   "title": "Storm Preparation - Senator Moody",
   "text": "SBA Disaster Assistance Loans – How to Apply Online:   www.sba.gov/funding-programs/disaster-assistance Online:   www.Farmers.gov/protection-recovery/hurricane Online:   www.hud.gov/disaster-resources If you need assistance with a federal agency, my office is here to help. You may submit a request for assistance by scanning the QR code below, visiting moody.senate.gov ,   or calling us toll-free in Florida at 866-630-7106. ·       Know evacuation routes and shelter locations; ·       Stock up on enough food, water and emergency supplies for the entire household for at least seven days, including: ·       Water (one gallon daily per person) and Non-Perishable Food"
  },
  {
   "id": 1090,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/storm-preparation/",
   "kind": "official_issues",
   "title": "Storm Preparation - Senator Moody",
   "text": "·       Non-Electric Can Openers, Paper Plates, and Plastic Utensils ·       Pillows, Blankets, and/or Sleeping Bags ·       Important Documents, such as Insurance, Medical, and Banking Records ·       First Aid Kits, Sunscreen, and Bug Spray ·       Battery-Powered or Hand-Crank Weather Radios ·        Check that storm-related products are hurricane-proof or impact-proof before making a purchase. ·       Follow instructions from local law enforcement and emergency management officials. ·       Stay away from windows and seek shelter."
  },
  {
   "id": 1091,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/storm-preparation/",
   "kind": "official_issues",
   "title": "Storm Preparation - Senator Moody",
   "text": "Every natural disaster or emergency provides an opportunity for unscrupulous individuals to try to take advantage of the crisis and prey on those in distress. Qualified contractors are in high demand following a disaster. If in need of a repair, follow these tips to find a reputable contractor: ·       Be wary of anyone who approaches unsolicited offering to work at a discount with supplies left from a previous job; ·       Have damage evaluated by the insurer before arranging repairs to ensure work will be covered; ·       Get at least three written, itemized estimates on repairs; ·       Research the company and its reputation with the Better Business Bureau at BBB.org ;"
  },
  {
   "id": 1092,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/storm-preparation/",
   "kind": "official_issues",
   "title": "Storm Preparation - Senator Moody",
   "text": "·       Verify the contractor’s license at MyFloridaLicense.com ; ·       Check for proof of insurance and verify with the insurer that the policy is current; ·       Read and understand the repair contract before signing; ·       Never pay the full amount of a repair up front and carefully consider before providing a large deposit; ·       Insist on releases from any liens that could be placed on the property prior to making final payment; and ·       Do not sign a certificate of completion until satisfied with the work performed."
  },
  {
   "id": 1093,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/storm-preparation/",
   "kind": "official_issues",
   "title": "Storm Preparation - Senator Moody",
   "text": "After a storm or other devastating event, you may wish to help those who suffered loss. Verify that charities are legitimate before donating and beware of solicitors using high-pressure tactics, such as demanding urgent donations or sharing limited information when soliciting donations."
  },
  {
   "id": 1094,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/sens-ashley-moody-and-rick-scott-introduce-bill-to-provide-tax-relief-for-skyrocketing-flood-insurance-costs/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Sens. Ashley Moody and Rick Scott Introduce Bill to Provide Tax Relief for Skyrocketing Flood Insurance Costs - Senator Moody",
   "text": "Sens. Ashley Moody and Rick Scott Introduce Bill to Provide Tax Relief for Skyrocketing Flood Insurance Costs - Senator Moody Sens. Ashley Moody and Rick Scott Introduce Bill to Provide Tax Relief for Skyrocketing Flood Insurance Costs"
  },
  {
   "id": 1095,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/sens-ashley-moody-and-rick-scott-introduce-bill-to-provide-tax-relief-for-skyrocketing-flood-insurance-costs/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Sens. Ashley Moody and Rick Scott Introduce Bill to Provide Tax Relief for Skyrocketing Flood Insurance Costs - Senator Moody",
   "text": "WASHINGTON, D.C. – Today, Senators Ashley Moody and Rick Scott introduced the Flood Insurance Relief Act to provide tax relief for Americans with a non-refundable tax deduction on flood insurance premiums paid through the National Flood Insurance Program (NFIP) or through private insurers. This bill will help ease the financial burden of rising flood insurance costs for hardworking Americans in Florida and across the nation. Congressman Byron Donalds is leading the companion legislation in the House of Representatives."
  },
  {
   "id": 1096,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/sens-ashley-moody-and-rick-scott-introduce-bill-to-provide-tax-relief-for-skyrocketing-flood-insurance-costs/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Sens. Ashley Moody and Rick Scott Introduce Bill to Provide Tax Relief for Skyrocketing Flood Insurance Costs - Senator Moody",
   "text": "Senator Ashley Moody said, “As I travel around the Sunshine State, one thing folks continue to tell me is that they are worried about the rising cost of flood insurance. That is why today, Senator Scott and I are working to ease the financial burden on Florida families by proposing a bill that would create a tax deduction on their flood insurance premiums. The Flood Insurance Relief Act is a critical solution that will directly benefit Floridians.”"
  },
  {
   "id": 1097,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/sens-ashley-moody-and-rick-scott-introduce-bill-to-provide-tax-relief-for-skyrocketing-flood-insurance-costs/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Sens. Ashley Moody and Rick Scott Introduce Bill to Provide Tax Relief for Skyrocketing Flood Insurance Costs - Senator Moody",
   "text": "Senator Rick Scott said, “Floridians know well that flood insurance can be a crucial but costly asset, and it is unacceptable that many are left struggling to find flood insurance coverage they can afford. Families shouldn’t have to choose between protecting their homes and putting food on the table. I’ve been working on several bills to fix the broken NFIP system and encourage private-sector participation to allow for a more robust, affordable flood insurance market, but we must do more to help families ASAP."
  },
  {
   "id": 1098,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/sens-ashley-moody-and-rick-scott-introduce-bill-to-provide-tax-relief-for-skyrocketing-flood-insurance-costs/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Sens. Ashley Moody and Rick Scott Introduce Bill to Provide Tax Relief for Skyrocketing Flood Insurance Costs - Senator Moody",
   "text": "My Flood Insurance Relief Act offers a practical way to directly ease the financial burden of flood insurance for families by allowing a tax deduction on their premiums, whether through the NFIP or the private market. I’m glad to have my fellow Floridians Senator Ashley Moody and Congressman Byron Donalds joining me in leading this effort.”"
  },
  {
   "id": 1099,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/sens-ashley-moody-and-rick-scott-introduce-bill-to-provide-tax-relief-for-skyrocketing-flood-insurance-costs/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Sens. Ashley Moody and Rick Scott Introduce Bill to Provide Tax Relief for Skyrocketing Flood Insurance Costs - Senator Moody",
   "text": "Congressman Byron Donalds said, “For far too long, the rising cost of flood insurance has crushed hardworking Floridians. This is unacceptable, this must change, and this critical issue must be addressed to ensure our economy works for all Americans. The time for action is now, and I’m proud to join Senator Rick Scott in introducing the Flood Insurance Relief Act to provide this overdue relief to policyholders across our Southwest Florida community, the Sunshine State, and the nation.”"
  },
  {
   "id": 1100,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/video-senator-moody-secures-more-than-2-3-billion-for-florida-communities-affected-by-disasters/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "VIDEO: Senator Moody Secures More than $2.3 BILLION for Florida Communities Affected by Disasters - Senator Moody",
   "text": "VIDEO: Senator Moody Secures More than $2.3 BILLION for Florida Communities Affected by Disasters - Senator Moody VIDEO: Senator Moody Secures More than $2.3 BILLION for Florida Communities Affected by Disasters FORT MYERS BEACH, Fla.— Senator Ashley Moody continues working to secure long-sought FEMA disaster funds for hard-hit Florida communities. Since taking office, Senator Moody has recovered more than $2.3 billion for Florida. Senator Moody stood with local emergency officials in Fort Myers Beach to break the news today on the peak day of hurricane season. Included in the $2.3 billion secured for statewide projects are more than $64.9 million for projects in Lee County."
  },
  {
   "id": 1101,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/video-senator-moody-secures-more-than-2-3-billion-for-florida-communities-affected-by-disasters/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "VIDEO: Senator Moody Secures More than $2.3 BILLION for Florida Communities Affected by Disasters - Senator Moody",
   "text": "“When I got to Washington, Florida was still owed billions of dollars for projects dating back years. We quickly went to work to cut through the bureaucracy and make sure our communities received the money they were owed. Today, we announced that our total recoveries have officially surpassed $2 billion. This is a major milestone, but our work isn’t over yet. We will keep working to deliver the federal support Floridians need,” said Senator Ashley Moody ."
  },
  {
   "id": 1102,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/video-senator-moody-secures-more-than-2-3-billion-for-florida-communities-affected-by-disasters/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "VIDEO: Senator Moody Secures More than $2.3 BILLION for Florida Communities Affected by Disasters - Senator Moody",
   "text": "Statewide, Senator Moody has secured more than $2.3 billion in FEMA public assistance funding. Included in these funds are more than $64.9 million secured for Lee County, with $5.5. million designated to help reconstruct the pier destroyed by Hurricane Ian. The replacement is planned to stretch roughly 1,000 feet into the Gulf, more than 70% longer than the one destroyed. These grants will be distributed along with the previously announced funds through FEMA’s Public Assistance and Hazard Mitigation Assistance programs to support more than 500 recovery projects across the state. This money is disbursed to the state and local communities for disaster recovery projects."
  },
  {
   "id": 1103,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/video-senator-moody-secures-more-than-2-3-billion-for-florida-communities-affected-by-disasters/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "VIDEO: Senator Moody Secures More than $2.3 BILLION for Florida Communities Affected by Disasters - Senator Moody",
   "text": "These projects include repairs to educational facilities, restoration of critical infrastructure, debris removal, and costs incurred during emergencies to protect life and property. Senator Moody introduced the  TRACK Act   (Transparency in Recovery Assistance & Claims Knowledge Act) to bring more transparency to the FEMA disaster aid process, which has now been passed into law. The TRACK Act mandates a status tracker on the FEMA website, so victims of a disaster have easily available knowledge and insight of their claim’s progress."
  },
  {
   "id": 1104,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/video-senator-moody-secures-more-than-2-3-billion-for-florida-communities-affected-by-disasters/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "VIDEO: Senator Moody Secures More than $2.3 BILLION for Florida Communities Affected by Disasters - Senator Moody",
   "text": "Sept. 10 represents the peak of the Atlantic Hurricane Season. Senator Moody created  webpage  aggregating hurricane preparedness and recovery resources for Floridians. Click  here  to learn more."
  },
  {
   "id": 1105,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/video-release-senator-moody-touts-1-5-billion-in-secured-fema-reimbursements-for-florida-and-passage-of-her-track-act-as-hurricane-season-looms/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "VIDEO RELEASE: Senator Moody Touts $1.5 Billion in Secured FEMA Reimbursements for Florida and Passage of Her TRACK Act as Hurricane Season Looms - Se",
   "text": "VIDEO RELEASE: Senator Moody Touts $1.5 Billion in Secured FEMA Reimbursements for Florida and Passage of Her TRACK Act as Hurricane Season Looms - Senator Moody VIDEO RELEASE: Senator Moody Touts $1.5 Billion in Secured FEMA Reimbursements for Florida and Passage of Her TRACK Act as Hurricane Season Looms"
  },
  {
   "id": 1106,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/video-release-senator-moody-touts-1-5-billion-in-secured-fema-reimbursements-for-florida-and-passage-of-her-track-act-as-hurricane-season-looms/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "VIDEO RELEASE: Senator Moody Touts $1.5 Billion in Secured FEMA Reimbursements for Florida and Passage of Her TRACK Act as Hurricane Season Looms - Se",
   "text": "BARTOW, Fla.— Senator Ashley Moody is touting the more than $1.5 billion secured for Florida in FEMA public assistance funding. Senator Moody worked to secure these funds to reimburse more than 500 projects around the state from hurricanes and other disasters dating back several years. Today in Bartow, Senator Moody also discussed efforts to improve transparency in disaster recovery through her TRACK Act and urged Floridians to be ready ahead of hurricane season."
  },
  {
   "id": 1107,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/video-release-senator-moody-touts-1-5-billion-in-secured-fema-reimbursements-for-florida-and-passage-of-her-track-act-as-hurricane-season-looms/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "VIDEO RELEASE: Senator Moody Touts $1.5 Billion in Secured FEMA Reimbursements for Florida and Passage of Her TRACK Act as Hurricane Season Looms - Se",
   "text": "“As hurricane season approaches, our work to help Floridians recover from storms or other natural disasters continues. I’m proud to have secured more than $1.5 billion in long-overdue FEMA funding to support communities across our state, while also advancing solutions like the TRACK Act to bring greater transparency to the recovery process,” said Senator Ashley Moody. Senator Moody worked with Department of Homeland Security to secure the commitment of funds for Florida disaster projects that had gone un-reimbursed."
  },
  {
   "id": 1108,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/video-release-senator-moody-touts-1-5-billion-in-secured-fema-reimbursements-for-florida-and-passage-of-her-track-act-as-hurricane-season-looms/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "VIDEO RELEASE: Senator Moody Touts $1.5 Billion in Secured FEMA Reimbursements for Florida and Passage of Her TRACK Act as Hurricane Season Looms - Se",
   "text": "Senator Moody pressed DHS Secretary Markwayne Mullin directly about the unfunded projects in Florida to secure the commitment. The grand total reimbursed by FEMA currently stands at $1,563,897,520. These projects include repairs to educational facilities, restoration of critical infrastructure, debris removal, and costs incurred during emergencies to protect life and property. The city of Bartow received more than $5.3 million for power and electrical system repair projects."
  },
  {
   "id": 1109,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/video-release-senator-moody-touts-1-5-billion-in-secured-fema-reimbursements-for-florida-and-passage-of-her-track-act-as-hurricane-season-looms/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "VIDEO RELEASE: Senator Moody Touts $1.5 Billion in Secured FEMA Reimbursements for Florida and Passage of Her TRACK Act as Hurricane Season Looms - Se",
   "text": "Senator Moody introduced the  TRACK Act  (Transparency in Recovery Assistance & Claims Knowledge Act) to bring more transparency to the FEMA disaster aid process and has now passed into law. The TRACK Bill mandates a status tracker on the FEMA website, so victims of a disaster have easily available knowledge and insight of their claim’s progress. Senator Moody is also urging Floridians ahead of the start of this year’s hurricane season to be ready to weather any storm: Build an emergency supply kit, with enough bottled water, nonperishable food, medications, and pet supplies to last at least seven days; Stay informed about potential storm threats by listening to local officials;"
  },
  {
   "id": 1110,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-moody",
   "url": "https://www.moody.senate.gov/press-releases/video-release-senator-moody-touts-1-5-billion-in-secured-fema-reimbursements-for-florida-and-passage-of-her-track-act-as-hurricane-season-looms/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "VIDEO RELEASE: Senator Moody Touts $1.5 Billion in Secured FEMA Reimbursements for Florida and Passage of Her TRACK Act as Hurricane Season Looms - Se",
   "text": "Create a family safety plan that outlines what you will do and where you will go in the event of a hurricane strike; and Reduce home hazards by placing large, heavy objects on lower shelves and removing objects from your yard that could become projectiles. To view Senator Moody’s full remarks at today’s event, click  here ."
  },
  {
   "id": 1111,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate Hardworking people should get to determine and shape what their communities look like and what their economies look like. – Alphonso Mayfield (Labor Leader and Fighter for all Floridians) A Government that Works for its People, Not Corporations Angie believes that the government should work for working people — not corporations, not billionaires, and not the political establishment in either party that keeps letting them win. Ask any Florida family what’s on their mind — whether they’re a Democrat, Republican, or don’t care much for either party — and you’ll hear the same thing: everything costs too much, and their paycheck can’t keep up."
  },
  {
   "id": 1112,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Since the pandemic, household expenses have jumped nearly a third. In Florida, the cost of living is climbing almost five times faster than it did a decade ago. Meanwhile, wages have stayed the same. Today, only a third of Floridians think our own state is affordable."
  },
  {
   "id": 1113,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "This isn’t an accident. It isn’t inevitable. While the average American is struggling, corporate landlords, insurance companies, and grocery chains have posted record profits. This year, Elon Musk became the world’s first trillionaire. And instead of delivering relief, politicians in Washington have spent months absorbed in a war that’s driving gas and energy prices even higher, while killing innocent civilians and American service people. Enough is enough. Angie will fight for the Working Families Guarantee A National Rent Freeze and Moratorium on Evictions A universal jobs program with inflation-adjusted wages Tax the billionaires so that everyone pays their fair share"
  },
  {
   "id": 1114,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Prioritize the needs of everyday Americans instead of spending trillions on war and violence overseas Foreign Policy rooted in Human Rights & Restraint Climate Action Matching the Scale of the Crisis The United States is the richest country on earth but doesn’t guarantee healthcare to all its people. Americans pay more for worse outcomes than anywhere else in the developed world. That’s not a healthcare system, it’s a protection racket for insurance and drug companies."
  },
  {
   "id": 1115,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Roughly 100 million Americans — about 4 in 10 adults — carry some form of medical debt, totaling at least $220 billion nationwide. People aren’t going into debt because they made bad choices; they’re going into debt because they got sick, had a baby or broke a bone. Medicare for All  that covers every person in America — free at the point of service, with no premiums, no deductibles, no copays, and no surprise bills. Comprehensive coverage , including dental, vision, hearing, mental health and substance use treatment, reproductive and maternity care, and prescription drugs. Capping prescription drug costs  and ending price gouging by drug companies."
  },
  {
   "id": 1116,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Protecting reproductive freedom , including the right to abortion, contraception, and IVF, free from political interference. Expanding home and community-based long-term care  so seniors and people with disabilities can age with dignity. Canceling the medical debt crushing families.  Canceling existing medical debt, wiping it off credit reports for good, and banning debt collectors from coming after patients for medical bill. Angie support senator Sanders’ bipartisan-backed Medical Debt Cancellation Act. Paid family and medical leave  for every worker in America, guaranteed by law Angie believes in Universal Child Care & Pre-K."
  },
  {
   "id": 1117,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Child care in America costs more than college tuition in most states. As a mom of 5, Angie knows this struggle deeply because she is experiencing it. Universal, high-quality child care and pre-kindergarten  for every family, regardless of income, capping costs so no family pays more than a small share of their income. Living wages for child care and early-childhood educators , who are among the most underpaid workers in the country despite doing some of its most important work. Universal school meals  so no child goes hungry during the school day. Angie believes in quality Public Education."
  },
  {
   "id": 1118,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Getting an education in America shouldn’t mean a lifetime of debt. About 43 million Americans now owe nearly $2 trillion in student loan debt. That’s about $43,500 per borrower, meaning people owe more for simply trying to get an education than they do on their cars or credit cards."
  },
  {
   "id": 1119,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "A degree that was once a ticket to the middle class has become a financial trap for millions of families, forcing young people to delay buying a home, starting a family, or saving for retirement just to keep up with payments on an education they were told they needed to get ahead. It’s not a personal failure; it’s the predictable result of a system that treats higher education as a private commodity instead of a public good. Tuition-free public college and trade school , and canceling student debt. Fully funding public K-12 schools   and increased teacher wages Expanding vocational and apprenticeship programs  that lead directly to good union jobs."
  },
  {
   "id": 1120,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Angie believes in housing you can actually afford. Rent is too high, homeownership is out of reach for millions, and Wall Street landlords are buying up housing stock and squeezing renters to enrich themselves. Florida is getting hit the hardest, and is now the worst state in the country for renters. On top of this, Florida homeowners now pay some of the highest insurance premiums in the nation — often as high as $10,000 a year — nearly three to four times the national average. Housing is a human right, not a speculative asset for the billionaire class. Massive investment in permanently affordable housing , building millions of new affordable units nationwide."
  },
  {
   "id": 1121,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "A national rent stabilization standard , just-cause eviction protections, and the right to counsel in eviction proceedings. Cracking down on corporate landlords and Wallstreet speculators  buying up single-family homes and driving up rents. Expanding Section 8 vouchers  so every eligible family can access one without languishing on a waitlist. Federal action on the property insurance crisis , including reinsurance backstops and stronger consumer protections, so Floridians aren’t priced out of their own homes by an insurance market that keeps failing them. Disaster resilience funding  to harden homes against hurricanes Angie believes in standing with workers & unions."
  },
  {
   "id": 1122,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "For too long, corporations have rigged labor law against working people. Angie was a labor organizer and will fight for the dignity of all workers. Passing the PRO Act  to make it easier to form a union and harder for corporations to bust one. Paid family and medical leave  for every worker in America, guaranteed by law. Raising the federal minimum wage  to a real living wage, indexed to inflation, for every worker, including immigrant and incarcerated workers. Ending “right to work” laws  and extending labor protections to workers historically excluded from them, including farmworkers and domestic workers."
  },
  {
   "id": 1123,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Protecting pensions and Social Security , and expanding benefits rather than cutting them. Fighting outsourcing  and trade policy that has hollowed out American manufacturing towns Angie believes in reining in big tech & AI companies. AI companies are racing to build massive data centers, and everyday families are getting stuck with the bill through higher electricity rates, strained water supplies and job cuts — while a handful of billionaires reap the profits."
  },
  {
   "id": 1124,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "On top of this, AI companies are rushing products to market that millions now use every day — — with little to no safety testing and no accountability when things go wrong. And things have gone wrong: families have testified before Congress after AI chatbots encouraged self-harm, failed to intervene during a mental health crisis, or in the most tragic cases, were linked to a child’s suicide. This isn’t a hypothetical harm. It’s already happened, and the companies that built these products have moved faster than the laws meant to hold them accountable. Making tech companies pay for the energy and water they use , not passing those costs on to ratepayers."
  },
  {
   "id": 1125,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "No new construction of data centers before there are real federal guardrails put in place , including environmental review and community input requirements. Protecting workers from AI-driven job displacement , including a real seat at the table for workers and unions as automation reshapes their industries. Breaking up concentrated tech monopolies  and strengthening antitrust enforcement against Big Tech. Protecting personal data privacy  and preventing AI-driven surveillance and discrimination."
  },
  {
   "id": 1126,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Real safety requirements for AI chatbots and companion apps , including mandatory protocols to detect suicidal ideation and connect users to real crisis resources — not silence, and not an AI pretending to be a therapist. Clear disclosure that a user is talking to a machine, not a person  — at the start of every conversation and repeated regularly, so no one, especially a child, is confused or manipulated into an unhealthy emotional dependency. Banning AI companies from letting chatbots impersonate licensed doctors, therapists, or attorneys Independent safety testing before AI products reach kids , not after the harm is already done."
  },
  {
   "id": 1127,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Funding for families and survivors  to pursue accountability, and support for the crisis-response infrastructure (like 988) that these products should be routing kids toward, not away from. Angie believes in a foreign policy rooted in diplomacy, human rights, and restraint. Angie believes American foreign policy should reflect the values of everyday Americans, not the interests of billionaire defense contractors. This year, lawmakers signed a $1.01 trillion defense budget while Americans at home struggle to afford housing and healthcare. End to the war in Iran and rebalance the federal budget toward investments in everyday people here at home"
  },
  {
   "id": 1128,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Uphold international law and institutions. Angie believes we should use the UN and multilateral diplomacy, not unilateral military action, as the first tool for resolving international conflicts, including in the Middle East. Build a future of lasting peace for Palestinians and Israelis in the region rooted in safety, equality and democracy for all people and respect for international law and human rights. This includes an end to US support for illegal settlements in the West Bank and upholding the ceasefire agreement in Gaza. Surge aid to places facing humanitarian crises such as: Gaza, the Westbank, Lebanon, Yemen, the Congo and Sudan"
  },
  {
   "id": 1129,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Uphold US law, including the The Leahy Law, which states U.S. taxpayer dollars and military assistance can never be used to enable violations of human rights, regardless of which country receives that aid. Restore U.S. participation and funding across UN agencies and public health programs that Americans and the rest of the world rely on. Restore humanitarian funding, including support that helps deliver food, medicine, and aid to refugees and children in crisis zones around the world. Angie believes in supporting human dignity, ending mass incarceration and deportation."
  },
  {
   "id": 1130,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "The US has the largest policing, incarceration and deportation system in the world. Millions of people — disproportionately Black, brown, and poor — are locked in cages or living in fear of a knock on the door, while corporations get rich off their suffering. This is not about safety. It is about control and profit. I don’t believe any person is illegal, and I don’t believe human beings should be treated as commodities in a system built to punish rather than to heal. Real safety comes from good jobs, strong schools, affordable housing, and healthcare for all — not from more cameras, more cages, and more agents tearing families apart."
  },
  {
   "id": 1131,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "It is time we had the courage to say it plainly: mass incarceration and mass deportation are moral failures, and I will fight in the United States Senate to end them. Ending mass incarceration , including federal decriminalization of marijuana and investment in treatment over incarceration for substance use. Demilitarizing policing  and investing in community-based public safety, violence prevention and crisis response A humane immigration system , including a swift path to citizenship for Dreamers and undocumented residents, and a moratorium on deportations pending a full audit of enforcement practices."
  },
  {
   "id": 1132,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Abolishing ICE and rebuilding immigration enforcement from scratch.  Since its creation in 2003, ICE has operated with almost no accountability — and that’s escalated into real tragedy, including U.S. citizens killed by federal immigration agents during enforcement surges in cities like Minneapolis. Angie believes an agency that has repeatedly shown it cannot be trusted with the power it has should not be reformed at the margins — it should be dismantled, with any legitimate immigration enforcement function rebuilt under new, accountable civilian oversight, due process protections, and a mission that reflects American values instead of terror tactics."
  },
  {
   "id": 1133,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Across the country, communities are pushing back against the rapid, unregulated spread of AI-powered surveillance technology — including automated license plate readers (ALPRs) like those sold by Flock Safety. These systems can track every vehicle that passes a camera, building a searchable record of where people go, when, and how often. That data can end up in the hands of federal immigration agents, out-of-state law enforcement, or bad actors — often without a warrant, without public knowledge, and without meaningful oversight. I believe you shouldn’t have to choose between public safety and your right to privacy."
  },
  {
   "id": 1134,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Requiring warrants for Surveillance Data Access. Law enforcement should not be able to search months of a person’s movements without judicial oversight. I will fight for federal standards requiring a warrant before ALPR or similar location data can be accessed in most circumstances. Ending Data Sharing with Federal Immigration Enforcement. Local police departments should not become a surveillance arm of ICE or CBP. I support legislation prohibiting the sharing of license plate and location data with federal immigration authorities absent a criminal warrant."
  },
  {
   "id": 1135,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Mandatory Data Deletion Windows. Indefinite retention of everyone’s movements — regardless of suspicion — is not acceptable. I will push for federal guidelines requiring surveillance data to be deleted within a short, defined window (in line with state laws that already require deletion within weeks) unless it is tied to an active investigation. Transparency and Public Accountability. Communities deserve to know when surveillance systems are installed, who has access to the data, how it’s used, and how often it leads to shared information with outside agencies. I support requiring public reporting and independent audits for any federally funded surveillance program."
  },
  {
   "id": 1136,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Ending Federal Funding for Mass Surveillance Systems Without Guardrails. Taxpayer dollars should not underwrite surveillance systems that lack basic privacy protections. I will advocate for tying federal grants and infrastructure funding to clear limits on ALPR use, data sharing, and retention. Protect Vulnerable Communities from Targeting. Surveillance systems have a documented history of disproportionately impacting immigrants, communities of color, and political dissidents. Any federal framework must include explicit protections against discriminatory use and misuse for political or retaliatory purposes."
  },
  {
   "id": 1137,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Local Control and Consent. Decisions about whether to deploy surveillance technology in a community should involve real public input — not be made unilaterally by a mayor’s office or a single department. I support requiring community consent processes before new surveillance contracts are signed or renewed with federal support. Angie believes in climate action that matches the scale of the crisis. The climate crisis is an existential threat, and the fossil fuel industry has spent decades lying about it while cashing in. Angie rejects the false choice between good jobs and a livable planet."
  },
  {
   "id": 1138,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "A bold, union-built transition to renewable energy , creating millions of good-paying, union jobs in wind, solar, and grid modernization, prioritizing the frontline communities that have borne the brunt of pollution for generations. Ending taxpayer subsidies for fossil fuel corporations  and making polluters pay for the damage they’ve caused. Rebuilding and hardening the electric grid , so it’s resilient, affordable, and ready for a clean-energy future Disaster resilience funding  to harden homes against hurricanes. Taking FEMA out of the Department of Homeland Security Angie believes in protecting and expanding democracy, and getting money out of politics."
  },
  {
   "id": 1139,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "When a handful of billionaires can spend hundreds of millions of dollars to influence an election and the average person gets one vote, that’s not a democracy for the many, but a corrupt government working for a few. Angie will fight to make this country a real democracy, so that this government works for all of us, not just the wealthy elite Overturning Citizens United  so corporations and billionaires can no longer buy elections with unlimited, often secret spending."
  },
  {
   "id": 1140,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Abolishing super PACs  and imposing real contribution limits. I suppor the  Abolish Super PACs Act  which would cap super PAC contributions at $5,000 — replacing today’s unlimited-money free-for-all with public financing that amplifies small-dollar donors instead of billionaire donors. Restoring and expanding the Voting Rights Act , including automatic voter registration for every American over 18, and ending racist voter suppression and burdensome voter ID laws. Ending partisan gerrymandering  with independent redistricting commissions. Making Election Day a national holiday , so working people don’t have to choose between their paycheck and their vote."
  },
  {
   "id": 1141,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Re-enfranchising Americans with felony convictions , restoring voting rights to the millions of Americans who have served their time and deserve to have their voice back. Public financing of elections , so candidates can run competitive campaigns without relying on corporate donors. Banning members of Congress from trading individual stocks  while in office. Closing the revolving door  between Congress, federal agencies, and the corporate lobbyists who work to influence them. Full transparency in campaign spending , ending dark money in our elections. Term limits and ethics reform for the Supreme Court , including binding ethics rules for all federal judges."
  },
  {
   "id": 1142,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Statehood for Washington, D.C. , so its residents finally get full representation in Congress. A real, binding process for Puerto Rico to determine its own political future  — statehood, independence, free association, or another path — decided by the people of Puerto Rico themselves, not dictated by Washington. More than 3 million American citizens on the island currently have no vote for president and no voting representation in Congress, despite paying certain federal taxes and serving in the U.S. military at high rates. Angie believes in making billionaires and corporations pay their fair share."
  },
  {
   "id": 1143,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Billionaire fortunes have exploded over the past few years while working families fall further behind on rent, groceries, and medical bills. Florida is home to more billionaires than almost any other state and meanwhile, everyday Floridians are struggling more than anyone with housing costs, healthcare cuts, job loss and inflation. Angie believes we can afford Medicare for All, universal child care, and a clean-energy future. What we can’t afford is letting the richest people in the country keep paying less in taxes than a nurse or a line cook."
  },
  {
   "id": 1144,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "A 5% annual wealth tax on billionaires.  I support Senator Sanders’  Make Billionaires Pay Their Fair Share Act , which would apply only to net worth above $1 billion — hitting fewer than 1,000 people in the entire country. Independent economists estimate it would raise roughly $4.4 trillion over ten years without raising taxes by a single dollar on anyone worth less than $1 billion. Direct relief for working families , funded by that revenue — including direct payments to households earning under $150,000 a year, expanding Medicare to cover dental, vision, and hearing, and building millions of affordable homes."
  },
  {
   "id": 1145,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Taxing capital gains the same as wages , so a billionaire’s stock portfolio isn’t taxed at a lower rate than a worker’s paycheck. Closing the loopholes that let profitable corporations pay $0 in federal income tax , including offshore tax havens and the “stepped-up basis” loophole that lets fortunes pass tax-free from one generation to the next. A federal asset registry and real IRS enforcement , so the ultra-wealthy can no longer hide assets or dodge audits — while ensuring the IRS stays focused on high-dollar evasion, not everyday taxpayers."
  },
  {
   "id": 1146,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Cracking down on corporate price gouging  in groceries, housing, and health care, where record corporate profits have tracked closely with what families are paying at the register. Angie believes in combatting anti-blackness, anti-semitism, Islamophobia, Nativism, transphobia, and all forms of hate."
  },
  {
   "id": 1147,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Hatred rooted in identity — whether directed at someone’s religion, race, gender or immigration status — has no place in American life. But hate is not a single, undifferentiated force. It takes distinct historical shapes and requires leaders who understand those differences. As a candidate for the United States Senate, I am committed to fighting antisemitism, Islamophobia, anti-immigrant hate, anti-Black racism and all forms of discrimination with the specificity and seriousness each demands, and to standing against hate crimes of every kind."
  },
  {
   "id": 1148,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Throughout history, the tools of division have shifted targets but repeated their logic – from the pogroms and killing of 6M Jewish people during the Holocaust to the Trans Atlantic Slave trade and Jim crow to the surveillence of Muslim and Arab communities after 9/11 to the violent attacks happening against immigrants in this country today. In each of these instances, the rich and powerful have worked to turn us against each other—so that instead of uniting around an agenda that guarantees everyone the chance at a healthy, thriving life, we’re left blaming our neighbors for problems they didn’t cause."
  },
  {
   "id": 1149,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "But we have far more in common with our neighbors — whatever their faith or background — than we do with the people counting on our division to keep their power intact. My campaign is committed to bringing all people together – across race, religion, geography and partisanship – to build a Florida where the safety, freedom and dignity of all people is protected."
  },
  {
   "id": 1150,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Real History in Our Schools. Support federal funding incentives for states and school districts that teach comprehensive history. Oppose federal or state efforts to ban books, censor curricula, or punish teachers for teaching accurate history, while supporting age-appropriate standards developed by educators and historians rather than political appointees. Hate Crime Enforcement. Support robust funding and enforcement for laws addressing hate crimes targeting. Ensure law enforcement agencies have training to recognize and respond to antisemitic, anti-Palestinian, Islamaphobic, anti-Black, anti-Immigrant and all threats and violence."
  },
  {
   "id": 1151,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/priorities/",
   "kind": "campaign_issues",
   "title": "Priorities - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Safe Campuses and Communities.  Ensure all students and community members can engage in public life, including on college campuses, free from harassment, intimidation, or violence — while protecting the rights of all students to engage in political speech and protest, including on Israel-Palestine. Angie Nixon did not rise through political machines or party gatekeepers. She built power in her community. From founding the Melanin Market to support local creators, to opening Natalie’s Nook to fight food insecurity, her work reflects a simple principle: This campaign is not asking for permission. Not from corporate donors. Not from party leadership. Not from anyone invested in the status quo."
  },
  {
   "id": 1152,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/meet-angie/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Meet Angie - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Meet Angie - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate Angie Nixon is a Democratic State Representative, union organizer, mother, and proven fighter born and raised in Jacksonville. In the State House, Angie has been a leading champion for working and middle class Floridians—from expanding childcare for thousands of families; to stopping a major grocery chain from gouging their prices; to leading the resistance to DeSantis’s unfair voting maps."
  },
  {
   "id": 1153,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/meet-angie/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Meet Angie - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Angie’s pathbreaking leadership includes serving as Executive Director of Florida for All, a statewide coalition that has registered tens of thousands of new voters while raising resources for campaigns and issue-based organizing across the state. At home in Jacksonville, she runs a bookstore and community hub focused on bringing healthy food and educational opportunities to local families."
  },
  {
   "id": 1154,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/meet-angie/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Meet Angie - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Angie’s leadership is rooted in her upbringing. She saw her mother work two jobs to make sure she and her brother never went hungry. Throughout elementary school, she was bused across town because her predominantly Black neighborhood school didn’t have adequate resources. Later, she tragically lost her favorite cousin to gun violence. With our state’s rich resources, we all deserve to thrive. Angie is fighting for better opportunities for our children. For lower costs and higher wages. For a government that stands up to corrupt billionaires and corporate greed—while opening the door to the people. For the heart and soul of our country."
  },
  {
