   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/the-latest/",
   "kind": "campaign_news",
   "title": "The Latest - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "U.S. Senate Candidate Angie Nixon Demands Sen. Ashley Moody Fight to Pass S. 4814 to Protect Florida’s Haitian Community MIAMI, FL – As hundreds of thousands of Haitian immigrants in Florida now face the terrifying threat of dangerous deportation after the sudden Trump Administration termination of Temporary Protected Status (TPS) this summer, U.S. Senate candidate Angie Nixon released the... U.S. Senate Candidate Angie Nixon Slams Trump Admin Lackeys Over “Leave America” Nonsense"
  },
  {
   "id": 1158,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/the-latest/",
   "kind": "campaign_news",
   "title": "The Latest - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "MIAMI – After a campaign rally where Vice President JD Vance teamed up with Ashley Moody to attack working-class Floridians and tell State Representative and U.S. Senate candidate Angie Nixon to ‘get the hell out’ of the United States, Rep.... Rep. Angie Nixon Condemns Trump Administration Decision To Kick 750,000+ Americans Off Health Insurance Following reports that the Trump administration is kicking over 750,000 Americans off of their Affordable Care Act (ACA) coverage under the guise of an “anti-fraud” initiative, U.S. Senate candidate Angie Nixon released the following statement: “Ripping health insurance away from..."
  },
  {
   "id": 1159,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/state-rep-angie-nixon-launchescampaign-for-u-s-senate/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "State Rep. Angie Nixon Launches Campaign for U.S. Senate - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "State Rep. Angie Nixon Launches Campaign for U.S. Senate - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate State Rep. Angie Nixon Launches Campaign for U.S. Senate TALLAHASSEE, FL – State Representative Angie Nixon (D-Jacksonville) announced her candidacy today for the U.S. Senate, launching a campaign to defeat appointed incumbent Ashley Moody in the 2026 elections. Rep. Nixon is running because Floridians are being crushed by an affordability crisis that Florida’s leadership has ignored for far too long."
  },
  {
   "id": 1160,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/state-rep-angie-nixon-launchescampaign-for-u-s-senate/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "State Rep. Angie Nixon Launches Campaign for U.S. Senate - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "“On my state listening tour over the last several months, I heard from Republicans, Independents, and Democrats who all said the same thing: We can’t afford to go on like this ,” said Rep. Nixon . “But these establishment politicians, including Ashley Moody, aren’t listening to us. Meanwhile, the cost of everything is exploding: groceries, healthcare, and childcare. Property insurance has doubled in the last four years, and housing costs are driving Floridians out of the towns they grew up in. Enough is enough. This isn’t a partisan issue."
  },
  {
   "id": 1161,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/state-rep-angie-nixon-launchescampaign-for-u-s-senate/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "State Rep. Angie Nixon Launches Campaign for U.S. Senate - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "We have to fix this affordability crisis, and we need and deserve a Senator who will fight to improve the lives of every Floridian, not just greedy billionaires.” Rep. Nixon, a fifth-generation Jacksonville native first elected to the Florida State House in 2020 , has built a reputation in Tallahassee as an outspoken fighter who is unafraid to confront corruption and powerful interests. She’s been a prominent champion for working and middle class Floridians, pushing to expand childcare for thousands of families and stopping a major grocery chain from price gouging."
  },
  {
   "id": 1162,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/state-rep-angie-nixon-launchescampaign-for-u-s-senate/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "State Rep. Angie Nixon Launches Campaign for U.S. Senate - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "In 2022, she led a high-profile floor protest against Governor DeSantis’ congressional redistricting scheme . In 2025, she sued the state after being denied access to the Everglades immigration detention facility , cruelly known as “Alligator Alcatraz,” and most recently introduced legislation requiring ICE and law enforcement agents to unmask and identify themselves on the job."
  },
  {
   "id": 1163,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/state-rep-angie-nixon-launchescampaign-for-u-s-senate/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "State Rep. Angie Nixon Launches Campaign for U.S. Senate - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "“As Ashley Moody runs around chasing headlines and playing into the culture wars that have nothing to do with daily reality, I’ve been working for the real people of Florida,” said Rep. Nixon . “Floridians didn’t elect Moody to the Senate, she was handed the seat. I know what it is to struggle. I know what it is to fight for everything you have. Moody doesn’t. It’s time for a Senator who cares more about how you pay your bills and get ahead than playing politics and taking care of billionaires.”"
  },
  {
   "id": 1164,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/state-rep-angie-nixon-launchescampaign-for-u-s-senate/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "State Rep. Angie Nixon Launches Campaign for U.S. Senate - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Angie’s leadership is rooted in her upbringing. She saw her mother work two jobs to make sure she and her brother never went hungry. Throughout elementary school, she was bused across the bridge because her predominantly Black neighborhood school didn’t have adequate resources. She lost her favorite cousin to gun violence. After graduating from the University of Florida in 2007, Angie went on to become a community organizer. Angie won her House seat in 2020 by defeating longtime incumbent Kimberly Daniels, a race few thought she could win."
  },
  {
   "id": 1165,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/state-rep-angie-nixon-launchescampaign-for-u-s-senate/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "State Rep. Angie Nixon Launches Campaign for U.S. Senate - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "She also served as the Executive Director of Florida for All, a statewide coalition that has registered tens of thousands of new voters while raising resources for campaigns and issue-based organizing across the state. She is a mother of five and a small business owner, running a bookstore and community hub that provides healthy food and educational opportunities to local families. “People are fed up,” said Rep. Nixon . “Everyone, not just Democrats. The Miami mayoral race is only one of the signs that a big shift is coming. People want leaders who will actually fight for them rather than fight each other on TV. It’s time. Change can’t wait any longer.”"
  },
  {
   "id": 1166,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/state-rep-angie-nixon-launchescampaign-for-u-s-senate/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "State Rep. Angie Nixon Launches Campaign for U.S. Senate - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Angie, whose campaign is headquartered in Jacksonville, will spend the coming weeks traveling around Florida talking to voters about their concerns. State Representative Angie Nixon is a Democratic member of the Florida House representing District 13 in Jacksonville. A solutions-oriented fighter for working families, Rep. Nixon focuses on issues that matter most to Floridians, like affordability, education, childcare, healthcare, and government transparency. She is a leading voice in the fight to put Floridians first and protect the democratic values of the Sunshine State."
  },
  {
   "id": 1167,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/angie-nixon-blasts-cruel-medicaid-cuts/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "U.S. Senate Candidate Angie Nixon Blasts Cruel Medicaid Cuts Kicking Nearly 177,000 Legal Immigrant Floridians Off Healthcare - Angie Nixon for U.S. S",
   "text": "U.S. Senate Candidate Angie Nixon Blasts Cruel Medicaid Cuts Kicking Nearly 177,000 Legal Immigrant Floridians Off Healthcare - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate U.S. Senate Candidate Angie Nixon Blasts Cruel Medicaid Cuts Kicking Nearly 177,000 Legal Immigrant Floridians Off Healthcare After new federal restrictions taking effect on Oct. 1  kicked nearly 177,000 legal immigrant Floridians off their Medicaid coverage , U.S. Senate candidate Angie Nixon released the following statement:"
  },
  {
   "id": 1168,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/angie-nixon-blasts-cruel-medicaid-cuts/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "U.S. Senate Candidate Angie Nixon Blasts Cruel Medicaid Cuts Kicking Nearly 177,000 Legal Immigrant Floridians Off Healthcare - Angie Nixon for U.S. S",
   "text": "“I know Florida’s current U.S. senators are used to screwing over working families when it comes to healthcare: Between Rick Scott’s  historic Medicare fraud  and Ashley Moody’s  $10 million Hope Florida scheme , treating healthcare like a personal slush fund is practically a tradition for them. But let’s be clear about who they’re targeting now: refugees who fled war, asylum seekers who escaped persecution, human trafficking victims, and Afghan interpreters who risked their lives helping our troops. They’re all here legally, yet politicians like Ashely Moody stripped away their health insurance."
  },
  {
   "id": 1169,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/angie-nixon-blasts-cruel-medicaid-cuts/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "U.S. Senate Candidate Angie Nixon Blasts Cruel Medicaid Cuts Kicking Nearly 177,000 Legal Immigrant Floridians Off Healthcare - Angie Nixon for U.S. S",
   "text": "“Kicking 177,000 legal immigrants off of Medicaid doesn’t stop them from getting sick or injured; it just forces them into emergency rooms for basic care, which drives up costs at a time when Florida hospitals are already facing hundreds of millions of dollars in unpaid healthcare costs. Absent Ashley and her extremist Republican friends created this problem, and now they’re trying to trick you into blaming your neighbors for the crisis instead."
  },
  {
   "id": 1170,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/angie-nixon-blasts-cruel-medicaid-cuts/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "U.S. Senate Candidate Angie Nixon Blasts Cruel Medicaid Cuts Kicking Nearly 177,000 Legal Immigrant Floridians Off Healthcare - Angie Nixon for U.S. S",
   "text": "“Healthcare is a human right, not a political weapon. That’s why I am unequivocally in favor of Medicare for All. No one should go bankrupt just to stay alive or get basic medical treatment. We need a senator who will fight to guarantee healthcare for everyone and end the corporate corruption that’s price-gouging our families.” To learn more about Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate, visit  angienixon.com ."
  },
  {
   "id": 1171,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/rep-angie-nixon-condemns-trump-administration-decision-to-kick-750000-americans-off-health-insurance/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Rep. Angie Nixon Condemns Trump Administration Decision To Kick 750,000+ Americans Off Health Insurance - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Rep. Angie Nixon Condemns Trump Administration Decision To Kick 750,000+ Americans Off Health Insurance - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate Rep. Angie Nixon Condemns Trump Administration Decision To Kick 750,000+ Americans Off Health Insurance Following  reports  that the Trump administration is kicking over 750,000 Americans off of their Affordable Care Act (ACA) coverage under the guise of an “anti-fraud” initiative, U.S. Senate candidate Angie Nixon released the following statement:"
  },
  {
   "id": 1172,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/rep-angie-nixon-condemns-trump-administration-decision-to-kick-750000-americans-off-health-insurance/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Rep. Angie Nixon Condemns Trump Administration Decision To Kick 750,000+ Americans Off Health Insurance - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "“Ripping health insurance away from over 750,000 Americans – roughly the combined population of Tampa and Orlando – is another direct attack on working-class families who are just trying to survive. It’s pure cruelty: using bureaucratic red tape to kick families to the curb while premiums double and insurance companies rake in record amounts of money for themselves. “Trump-aligned Ashley Moody has spent her career playing this same game: supporting Medicaid cuts and letting insurance monopolies price-gouge us as they donate to her campaign. In fact, she’s already ripped healthcare away from 440,000 Floridians because she’s corrupt and bad at her job."
  },
  {
   "id": 1173,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://angienixon.com/rep-angie-nixon-condemns-trump-administration-decision-to-kick-750000-americans-off-health-insurance/",
   "kind": "press_release",
   "title": "Rep. Angie Nixon Condemns Trump Administration Decision To Kick 750,000+ Americans Off Health Insurance - Angie Nixon for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "“Floridians deserve a leader who actually delivers results. In the U.S. Senate, I will take on the corporate greed driving up our costs and work to ensure every working family can see a doctor without going broke.” To learn more about Angie and join the movement, visit  angienixon.com ."
  },
  {
   "id": 1174,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://www.tampabay28.com/news/election-2026/meet-the-candidates-questionnaire-for-florida-us-senate",
   "kind": "questionnaire",
   "title": "Meet the candidates: Questionnaire for Florida US Senate",
   "text": "Meet the candidates: Questionnaire for Florida US Senate Meet the candidates: Questionnaire for Florida US Senate Tampa Bay 28 invited more than 200 candidates running in the Aug. 18, 2026, primary election across our five-county area to submit the following: a candidate photo, a 100-word biography, and responses to three questions: In your own words, what differentiates you from your opponents? Explain what you see as the most important issue facing our community and how you are uniquely qualified to address that issue? The following candidates responded to our questionnaire."
  },
  {
   "id": 1175,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://www.tampabay28.com/news/election-2026/meet-the-candidates-questionnaire-for-florida-us-senate",
   "kind": "questionnaire",
   "title": "Meet the candidates: Questionnaire for Florida US Senate",
   "text": "I am a Democratic State Representative from Jacksonville, a mother, union organizer, and small business owner. My leadership is rooted in community and lived experience. I grew up watching my mom work two jobs to get by, lost a cousin to gun violence, and currently run a small business. As a state representative, I have worked on legislation expanding childcare access, addressing price gouging, and challenging Florida’s rigged voting maps. Before this, I led the statewide coalition called Florida for All and have helped register tens of thousands of new voters. Throughout my career, I’ve built power from the ground up focused on the needs of Floridians."
  },
  {
   "id": 1176,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://www.tampabay28.com/news/election-2026/meet-the-candidates-questionnaire-for-florida-us-senate",
   "kind": "questionnaire",
   "title": "Meet the candidates: Questionnaire for Florida US Senate",
   "text": "a. I am running for office to address the immediate and urgent needs that the people of Florida are facing. My focus is on lowering everyday costs, creating a healthcare system that works for people, and protecting the benefits such as Social Security, Medicare, Medicaid, the VA. b. Additionally, I will fight to make childcare affordable and accessible because this is an economic investment in our people and communities. People are struggling to put food on their tables and keep a roof over their heads while politicians in Washington are looking out for corporations. I’m running to make sure the government works for us and not against us."
  },
  {
   "id": 1177,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://www.tampabay28.com/news/election-2026/meet-the-candidates-questionnaire-for-florida-us-senate",
   "kind": "questionnaire",
   "title": "Meet the candidates: Questionnaire for Florida US Senate",
   "text": "In your own words, what differentiates you from your opponents? a. I am the only candidate in this race with a proven track record of championing the issues that actually impact ordinary Floridians and delivering legislative results. For the past 6 years, I have remained laser focused on the needs of Floridians and my legislative agenda has reflected that. I have delivered on things like affordable childcare, wage raises, and home insurance in a bipartisan way in the Florida Legislature. We are in a time that requires leaders who will fight through anything for the needs of the people."
  },
  {
   "id": 1178,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-nixon",
   "url": "https://www.tampabay28.com/news/election-2026/meet-the-candidates-questionnaire-for-florida-us-senate",
   "kind": "questionnaire",
   "title": "Meet the candidates: Questionnaire for Florida US Senate",
   "text": "b. Effective leadership requires coalition-building without compromising core values. My campaign is a grassroots, pro-labor movement that answers to the people. Explain what you see as the most important issue facing our community and how are you uniquely qualified to address that issue? a. The most important issue facing Floridians is the cost of living. People cannot afford to live, raise a family, and retire here, and that is wrong. A public servant must listen to their constituents' needs and act upon them. I have done this on a state level and will continue to do so as your US Senator representing the people of Florida."
  },
