  {
   "id": 1187,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Library of Congress Web Archiving Program Sarah's Calls For Help Were Not a Crime , Justice Network Email This BlogThis! Share to X Share to Facebook Share to Pinterest United States Election 2026 Web Archive , Neil J. Gillespie Candidate Survey Responses to Ballotpedia Neil J. Gillespie Candidate Survey Responses to Ballotpedia"
  },
  {
   "id": 1188,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "I am \"No Party Neil\", Neil J. Gillespie, a No Party Affiliation Candidate (NPA) for United States Senator for Florida in the general election set for November 3, 2026. I am motivated to run for office because of lawfare and lack of due process in our state and federal courts. Our first president, George Washington, warned us about political parties in his Farewell Address. That is why I am a \"No Party Affiliation\" (NPA) candidate. Washington emphasized three points: 1) The importance of unity as a Nation; 2) The danger of party loyalty over the interests of our Nation; 3) The danger of foreign entanglements."
  },
  {
   "id": 1189,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Regarding experience, I am founder and director of Justice Network, engaged in advocacy, education, news gathering and dissemination, and helping people fight injustice. I moved to Florida from Pennsylvania in 1993 where I was a licensed motor vehicle dealer. I am a capitalist. I am a graduate of the Wharton School, Evening Division, of the University of Pennsylvania (ABA), and of The Evergreen State College (BA). If elected, my top priorities are restore integrity in our government through the separation of powers doctrine. U.S. District Judge Pamela Chen says \"The concept of separation of powers is what makes America great."
  },
  {
   "id": 1190,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "It is absolutely the genius of our democracy\" Also the First Amendment: Freedom of speech and the press, separation of church & state, and redress of grievances, including the writ of habeas corpus. Please list below 3 key messages of your campaign. What are the main points you want voters to remember about your goals for your time in office?"
  },
  {
   "id": 1191,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "1. Restore checks and balances in government, separation of powers. Lawyers admitted to practice are officers of the court, part of the judicial branch of government, and must not serve in elected office in the legislature or executive branch. Joe Biden and Kamala Harris, are lawyers admitted to practice, and who wrongly served as president and vice president, created the current immigration problem with open borders. Florida Governor Ron DeSantis, a lawyer admitted to practice, is wrongly serving in the executive (as governor), and was able to wrongly take $10 million in taxpayer money, his \"cherry on top\", for his wife's charity."
  },
  {
   "id": 1192,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "2. Health care reform. I was born needing craniofacial surgery but my insurance denied coverage for surgery when I was age 18 under a preexisting condition clause. I propose national health coverage, with the ability to opt-out. Trial Lawyers add excessive costs, and force doctors to practice defensive medicine. See my Healthcare page https://www.nosue.org/healthcare/ Five other capitalist democracies -- the United Kingdom, Japan, Germany, Taiwan and Switzerland -- deliver health care to their people. We The People can learn from their successes and their failures."
  },
  {
   "id": 1193,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "House and Senate members are allowed to purchase health insurance offered through the Federal Employees Health Benefits Program, which covers more than 8 million federal workers."
  },
  {
   "id": 1194,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "3. Guarantee the safety of Jews in the United States. America is the promised land that defeated fascism in Europe in 1945. Hold Bibi responsible for allowing October 7th to happen, and for the war on Iran. Iran is Bibi's war, and it is a disaster. Unfortunately, Israel cannot protect Jews. Its wars are creating antisemitism worldwide. Prime Minister Yitzhak Rabin made peace with the Palestinians (Oslo Accords). But on Nov-04-1995, an Israeli, Yigal Amir, murdered Rabin, ending the peace plan. Most of my family (Catholic) came to America from Ireland. My maternal great-grandmother was Jewish. We are not a \"Christian Nation\" as some claim."
  },
  {
   "id": 1195,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Catholics, Jews, Hindus, and Muslims are not \"Christians\". The video below was not part of my response. What areas of public policy are you personally passionate about?"
  },
  {
   "id": 1196,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Immigrants are essential for the U.S. economy. We need qualified, vetted, immigrants legally present in America. The de facto open border policy of the Biden administration was wrong. The Biden immigration policy has benefited the legal profession, not the American People. Business is great for immigration lawyers. I support secure boarders. We need to know who is in our county, who is in our home. Immigrants' background must be vetted. I support the lawful removal of people who enter the United States illegally, but not the spectacle created by activists confronting ICE. I also support a path to citizenship for immigrants who follow the rules."
  },
  {
   "id": 1197,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "We need to know who is voting in our elections. We must end birth tourism. What organizations or individuals have endorsed your campaign?"
  },
  {
   "id": 1198,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "The United States Library of Congress has selected my website for inclusion in the United States Election 2026 Web Archive, which is part of a larger collection of historically and culturally significant websites that have been designated for preservation. The following URL has been selected: https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/ The Library of Congress or its agent will engage in the collection of content from my website at regular intervals over time. In order to properly archive the above URL, the Library of Congress may archive other portions of the website and public content that your page links to on third party sites such as social media platforms."
  },
  {
   "id": 1199,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "This content will be available to researchers at Library facilities. The video below was not part of my response. Prosecutorial Misconduct Cuts Both Ways in Marion County Florida Email This BlogThis! Share to X Share to Facebook Share to Pinterest Neil J. Gillespie Candidate Survey Responses to League of Women Voters Palm Beach County Neil J. Gillespie Candidate Survey Responses to League of Women Voters Palm Beach County 1. What reforms to the US immigration system do you support? Why?"
  },
  {
   "id": 1200,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Immigrants are essential for the U.S. economy. We need qualified, vetted, immigrants legally present in America. The de facto open border policy of the Biden administration was wrong. The Biden immigration policy has benefited the legal profession, not the American People. Business is great for immigration lawyers. But some like former lawyer Alexandra Lozano, \" La Luz del Camino Legal \", defrauded her clients. Most of my family came to America from Ireland. My maternal great-grandmother was Jewish. I have worked with and support immigrants are naturalized citizens. In Pennsylvania I was a licensed motor vehicle dealer with many immigrant customers."
  },
  {
   "id": 1201,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "I support secure boarders because we need to know who is in our county, who is in our home. Immigrants' background must be vetted. I support the lawful removal of people who enter the United States illegally, but not the spectacle created by activists confronting ICE. I also support a path to citizenship for immigrants who follow the rules. Photo: Neil Gillespie October 20, 2022 working at NPSG Caddell at Walmart Brooksville FL. This photo was provided to Ballotpedia but not published because it is over two years old. 2. Name your top two legislative priorities for the next Congressional term."
  },
  {
   "id": 1202,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "My top three legislative priorities (not two) for the next congress: 1. Restore checks and balances in government, separation of powers. Lawyers admitted to practice are officers of the court, part of the judicial branch of government, and must not serve in elected office in the legislature or executive branch. 2. Health care reform . I was born needing craniofacial surgery but my insurance denied coverage for surgery when I was age 18 under a preexisting condition clause. I propose national health coverage, with the ability to opt-out. Trial Lawers add excessive costs, and force doctors to practice defensive medicine. 3. Guarantee the safety of Jews in the United States."
  },
  {
   "id": 1203,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "America is the promised land that defeated fascism in Europe in 1945 . Unfortunately, Israel cannot protect Jews. Its wars are creating antisemitism worldwide. Prime Minister YitzhakRabin made peace with the Palestinians (Oslo Accords). But on Nov-04-1995, an Israeli, Yigal Amir, murdered Rabin , ending the peace plan. The video below was not part of my response. 3. \"Freedom of speech\" is included in the First Amendment to the U.S. Constitution. Exactly what does \"Freedom of Speech\" mean to you?"
  },
  {
   "id": 1204,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Freedom of speech is the right to express opinions and ideas without fear. First Amendment: \"Congress shall make no law respecting an establishment of religion, or prohibiting the free exercise thereof; or abridging the freedom of speech, or of the press; or the right of the people peaceably to assemble, and to petition the Government for a redress of grievances.\" That means we are not a \"Christian Nation\" as some claim. Catholics, Jews, Hindus, and Muslims are not \"Christians\". Also, the right to \"petition the Government for a redress of grievances\" is under threat with our current broken court system."
  },
  {
   "id": 1205,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Twenty-one years ago (in 2005) I sued a Florida law firm for stealing money from my settlement in a civil case. The courts could not resolve the case after 20 years, so I dropped it in 2025. Too many people end up suing their crooked lawyers. One well-known case is \" Take Care of Maya \", Maya Kowalski's family, who sued their former attorneys over alleged mishandling of settlement funds. 4. What role do you believe the federal government should play in education at the pre-school level, K-12 level and higher education?"
  },
  {
   "id": 1206,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Parents have the most important role in the education of their children. My parents sent me to Catholic elementary school (grades 1-8) and Catholic high school (grades 9-12) where I was raised in Levittown, PA. The state, when acting \" in loco parentis \", is responsible for the child's safely at school. In higher education, students age 18 and older are generally considered adults for legal and institutional purposes. On September 27, 2016, I wrote President Obama about an African-American schoolgirl in Ocala who needed assistance attending public school, which is a federally protected activity under 18 U.S.C. § 245(b)(2)(A)."
  },
  {
   "id": 1207,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "The Ocala Star-Banner reported a racial incident at West Port High School where 3 students taunted the Black student while waiving Con-federate flags. The 15 year-old African-American victim being intimidated by whites was wrongly cited by the police in lieu of arrest. Obama never responded. Florida AG Pam Bondi failed to classify this as a hate crime. (FS 775.085) Note: The League of Women Voters Palm Beach County only published 4 of the 7 responses to questions presented to the candidates. Here are my 3 responses that were not published : 5. Do you believe climate change is a financial threat to the economy of the nation? Why or why not?"
  },
  {
   "id": 1208,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Climate change itself is not a financial threat to the economy, but is an issue to be managed. Extreme reaction to climate change is a financial threat. Obama's 2009 \"Cash for Clunkers\" program is an example of an extreme reaction. The program scrapped 677,081 vehicles, which was a terrible waste. The Ford Explorer 4WD was the program's top trade-in according to the U.S. DoT. (Wikipedia). Americans still want this type of vehicle. This program \"still frustrates car enthusiasts, mechanics, collectors, and budget-minded drivers more than 15 years later. [677,081] vehicles were deliberately destroyed under the Cash for Clunkers program."
  },
  {
   "id": 1209,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Not recycled after they wore out, not sold to families who needed affordable transportation, and not donated to people struggling to get by. They were intentionally taken out of service and reduced to scrap.\" (Yahoo Auto). Instead of scrapping vehicles, Obama could have provided checks to people to buy new vehicles and help the struggling auto industry. 6. Who has the right, Congress or the President, to oversee federal agencies? U.S. District Judge Pamela Chen said, in Court Shorts, Separation of Powers : \"This concept of separation of powers is what makes America great. It is absolutely the genius of our democracy.\""
  },
  {
   "id": 1210,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "The duty to oversee federal agencies is found in the Constitution. Currently our government is corrupted by a failure of checks and balances, a failure of separation of powers in government. Lawyers admitted to practice are officers of the court, part of the judicial branch of government, and must not serve in elected office in the legislature or the executive branch. Joe Biden and Kamala Harris, lawyers admitted to practice, and who wrongly served as president and vice president, created the current immigration problem with open borders."
  },
  {
   "id": 1211,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Florida Governor Ron DeSantis, a lawyer admitted to practice, is wrongly serving in the executive (as governor), and was able to wrongly take $10 million in taxpayer money, his \"cherry on top\", for his wife's charity. 7. If documentary proof of US citizenship becomes necessary in order to register to vote, how would you help those citizens, especially women, who no longer have or don’t have easy and affordable access to documents to prove citizenship, such as certified birth and marriage certificates?"
  },
  {
   "id": 1212,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "US citizenship comes with responsibilities. Take action now to get the documents needed to prove citizenship. The best way to prove US citizenship may be your US Passport. Keep your US Passport current. The State Department issues passports and can assist citizens. Perhaps the State Department should serve as a repository for the documents needed to prove citizenship, such as certified birth and marriage certificates. Proof of citizenship is important for secure elections, and a secure border. We The People need to know who is in our country, our home, and who is voting in our elections. The video below was not part of my response."
  },
  {
   "id": 1213,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "\"Origins of a Genocide\": Al Jazeera’s Marwan Bishara on \"Twelve Days That Shook the Middle East , Democracy NOW! Email This BlogThis! Share to X Share to Facebook Share to Pinterest federally protected activity 18 U.S.C. § 245(b)(2)(A) , Neil J. Gillespie Candidate Survey Responses to Daytona Regional Chamber of Commerce 2026 General Elections Voter Guide Neil J. Gillespie Candidate Survey Responses to Daytona Regional Chamber of Commerce 2026 General Elections Voter Guide 1. What motivated you to run for office?"
  },
  {
   "id": 1214,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Lawfare and lack of due process in our state and federal courts. Our first president, George Washington, warned us about political parties in his Farewell Address. That is why I am a \"No Party Affiliation\" (NPA) candidate. Washington emphasized three points: 1) The importance of unity as a Nation; 2) The danger of party loyalty over the interests of our Nation; 3) The danger of foreign entanglements. We The People Can Do Better. Photo: Neil J. Gillespie, University of Pennsylvania, Wharton School Graduation, May 21, 1989. This photo was provided to Ballotpedia but not published because it is over 2 years old."
  },
  {
   "id": 1215,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "2. What is your professional experience, and how does that experience qualify you for the office you are seeking? I am founder and director of Justice Network, engaged in advocacy, education, news gathering and dissemination, and helping people fight injustice. I moved to Florida from Pennsylvania in 1993 where I was a licensed motor vehicle dealer. I am a capitalist. I am a graduate of the Wharton School, Evening Division, of the University of Pennsylvania (ABA), and of The Evergreen State College (BA). We The People Can Do Better. 3. If elected, what will be your top priorities?"
  },
  {
   "id": 1216,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Restore integrity in our government through the separation of powers doctrine. U.S. District Judge Pamela Chen says \"The concept of separation of powers is what makes America great. It is absolutely the genius of our democracy\". Also the First Amendment: Freedom of speech and the press, separation of church and state, freedom of peaceful assembly, and right to petition the Government for a redress of grievances, including the writ of habeas corpus. We The People Can Do Better. Email This BlogThis! Share to X Share to Facebook Share to Pinterest Hello Florida voters, yesterday we had a primary election."
  },
  {
   "id": 1217,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "I am \"No Party Neil\", Neil J. Gillespie, a No Party Affiliation Candidate for the United States Senate for Florida in the general election November 3rd. Florida is a closed primary state. Therefore, my name as a No Party Affiliation candidate did not appear on the primary ballot. Today from my campaign office in Ocala Florida I am officially announcing my campaign. I also want to congratulate my opponent Angie Nixon for winning the Democrat Senate nomination . I also want to congratulate Ashley Moody for winning the Republican Senate nomination."
  },
  {
   "id": 1218,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "This is now a three way race for the U.S. Senate. Florida voters now have a choice beyond partisan politics. President George Washington warned against political parties in his Farewell Address. Washington urged Americans to always place the interests of the nation over their political and regional affiliations. Florida voters now have a choice beyond partisan politics. With your vote, I will be your independent voice in the Senate of the United States. I am running for public office in part because of lawfare and lack of due process in our state and federal courts."
  },
  {
   "id": 1219,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "To my fellow Florida voters, you now have a choice. I am a working class capitalist. I am not a socialist like my opponent Ms. Nixon. And I am not a lawyer like Ashley Moody beholden to The Florida Bar, and the legal establishment. We are done with that nonsense. Vote for me, No Party Neil Gillespie on November 3rd for U.S. Senate. Thank you. Paid for by Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate for Florida Email This BlogThis! Share to X Share to Facebook Share to Pinterest PRESS RELEASE No Party Neil U.S. Senate Florida PRESS RELEASE No Party Neil for U.S. Senate Florida (updated Jul-29-2026)"
  },
  {
   "id": 1220,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "I am \"No Party Neil\", Neil J. Gillespie, a No Party Affiliation Candidate (NPA) for United States Senator for Florida in the general election set for November 3, 2026. President George Washington warned against political parties in his Farewell Address. Washington urged Americans to always place the interests of the nation over their political and regional affiliations . Florida is a closed primary state. Therefore, my name as a NPA candidate will not appear on the primary election ballot for the partisan primary election set for August 18, 2026. There are six candidates in the partisan primary election for U.S. Senate, 4 Republicans and 2 Democrats:"
  },
  {
   "id": 1221,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "R: Chris Gleason; Ashley Moody; Neelam Perry; Ernie Rivera On August 19, 2026, the day after the partisan primary election, I plan to officially launch my campaign. I believe this is a more effective strategy, against the general election candidates on November 3, 2026, rather than campaigning against 6 partisan primary candidates, where I am not even on the ballot! The Florida Division of Elections emailed me on July 15, 2026 in response to my observation that Ballotpedia and Wikipedia claim this is a special election : Thank you for your message. This election will be a General election (not special) per s. 100.161 and 100.111(1)(a), Florida Statutes."
  },
  {
   "id": 1222,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "There were more than 28 months remaining on Sen. Rubio’s vacated term and therefore Sen. Moody’s appointed term is only through the 2026 general election, at which a person will be elected to fill the remainder of Rubio’s term to 1/3/2029. See Art. IV, s. 1 (f), Florida Constitution and 100.111(1)(a), Florida Statutes, which reads:"
  },
  {
   "id": 1223,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "(1)(a) If any vacancy occurs in any office which is required to be filled pursuant to s. 1(f), Art. IV of the State Constitution and the remainder of the term of such office is 28 months or longer, then at the next general election a person shall be elected to fill the unexpired portion of such term, commencing on the first Tuesday after the first Monday following such general election. The person elected at the 2028 election will put the terms back on track and that person will serve a full 6 years. Therefore, if elected on November 3, 2026, I would be the incumbent candidate in 2028."
  },
  {
   "id": 1224,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "On May 4, 2026, I gave notice to the Federal Election Commission that I suspended my 2028 campaign for president while I am running for United States Senator. There is an exception to the closed primary rule. An article by political consultant Jeff Carman of the Manatee Patriots explains The Florida State Representative Universal Primary Contest . \"Florida is a Closed Primary state, which means that for a voter to choose the party nominee for a political party in a Partisan Elected race, the voter must be a registered voter of that political party to participate. There are however opportunities for voters not registered as a Democrat or a Republican to vote."
  },
  {
   "id": 1225,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "They may vote in all Non-Partisan (at least in name) or no party affiliated races which under the Florida Constitution includes All Municipal City Council & Commission Races, County School Board Members (Presently) and almost all Judicial races from retention of Supreme Court members, Circuit and District Courts, County Judges and races like Soil and Water Conservation Board, Mosquito Control, Fire Districts, and Community Development Districts."
  },
  {
   "id": 1226,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "In rare instances, a scenario will come to fruition where all candidates that qualify in a partisan election are of ONE political party and no other candidates qualify that would appear on a ballot in the general election from another major political party or a write in candidate. In this scenario, a Universal Primary Contest occurs. When all candidates for an office have the same party affiliation and the winner will have no opposition in the general election, all voters, regardless of party affiliation, will have the opportunity to vote in this race…\""
  },
  {
   "id": 1227,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Marion County, Florida has a Universal Primary Contest on August 18, 2026 for State Representative District 24 because the Democrat Party failed field a candidate. Ballotpedia reports , \"The Democratic primary scheduled for August 18, 2026, was canceled.\" The Republican Party has two candidates: Incumbent Rep. Ryan Chamberlin (R-Belleview) and a Republican candidate challenger, Scott Wilkins . The article by Jeffrey Carman is attached, along with my personal sample ballot showing the Universal Primary Contest scheduled for August 18, 2026 between Ryan Chamberlin and Scott Wilkins. The Marion County Supervisor of Elections provided my sample ballot."
  },
  {
   "id": 1228,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "My responses to the 2026 Daytona Regional Chamber of Commerce voter guide questionnaire are posted here as a 2026 candidate for United States Senate for Florida . Here are links to some of my online presence: 2025 Federal Election Lawsuit: Mayor, City of Ocala, FL Neil J. Gillespie, updated July 25, 2026 Paid for by Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate, Committee ID: C00943399 General George Washington. Image Credit: Creative Commons. Email This BlogThis! Share to X Share to Facebook Share to Pinterest Notice to The Florida Bar: Anti-Weaponization Fund Federal Lawsuit Notice to The Florida Bar: Anti-Weaponization Fund Federal Lawsuit Mr. Joshua E. Doyle, Executive Director , The Florida Bar"
  },
  {
