   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "Cc: Mr. Richard Courtemanche, Deputy General Counsel, The Florida Bar It has come to my attention that Judge Kathleen Williams may have referred Florida attorney Alejandro Brito, Bar # 98442, to the Florida Bar for consideration on whether Brito should be disciplined in light of the findings in the new order in Trump v IRS , according to a post by David Oscar Markus on his SDFLA blog"
  },
  {
   "id": 1230,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "In defense of Mr. Brito, and to offer myself as a substitute plaintiff-intervenor , I submit my response to the Federal Election Commission of June 25, 2025 , which PDF is attached, and found on the FEC website , and my blog Neil 2028 . Please note I have a claim against the IRS, and a claim against the State of Florida, the DeSantis administration, and the Biden administration, for lawfare involving Fla. Stat. sec. 934.03. WRITTEN OBJECTION to the Federal Election Commission , Administrative Termination of NEIL J. GILLESPIE FOR PRESIDENT Campaign Committee"
  },
  {
   "id": 1231,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "\"I plan to intervene in Trump v IRS, USDC, SDFL Case No. 1.26-cv-20609 (Anti-Weaponization Fund) U.S. Judge Kathleen Williams and Magistrate Judge Enjoliqué Lett presiding. In Dunn v Trump et al, USCD, District of Columbia Case No. 1.26-cv-01719 , U.S. Judge Richard Leon presiding, two Capital Policemen, Harry Dunn and Daniel Hodges, sued over the Anti-Weaponization Fund. Officer Dunn and Officer Hodges have a right to know the FEC failed to act on a legitimate Complaint of Election Fraud in the 2020 Presidential Election . Harry Dunn and Daniel Hodges (photo added)"
  },
  {
   "id": 1232,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "In Andrew Floyd v DOJ, USDC, Eastern Division Virginia, Case No. 1.26-cv-1399 , Plaintiffs Andrew Floyd, Jonathan Caravello, City of New Haven, National Abortion Federation, and Common Cause, contend \"The Department of Justice and the Department of Treasury have created a $1.776 billion slush fund—from taxpayer dollars—to dispense payment to those the Trump-Vance administration favors. Since its inception, this fund has been on a collision course with the United States Constitution.\" No. My complaint shows a lawyer admitted to practice law is an officer of the court, and a member of the judicial branch of government, and constitutionally prohibited from serving as vice president."
  },
  {
   "id": 1233,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "That means J.D. Vance, as a lawyer admitted to practice, should be removed from office. U.S. Judge Leonie Brinkema and Magistrate Judge Ivan Davis are presiding."
  },
  {
   "id": 1234,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "In two other cases, Perkins Coie LLP v DOJ et al, DC Circuit Court of Appeal No. 25-5241, Trial Judge Beryl Howell; USDC, District of Columbia, Case No. 1:25-cv-00716-BAH , and American Bar Association (ABA) v Trump DOJ et al, DC Circuit Court of Appeal No. 25-5128 Trial Judge Amir H. Ali, USDC-District of Columbia Case No. 1.25-cv-01888 , each of those cases argue separation of powers prevents President Trump from jurisdiction over lawyers and law firms. The ABA even cites the same case I rely upon: Ex parte Garland, 71 U.S. 333 (1866) . The enclosed Transcript of the CBS News 60 Minutes episode with Scott Pelly, The Rule of Law , May 2, 2025, shows this quote by John Keker:"
  },
  {
   "id": 1235,
   "candidate_id": "us-senate-fl-gillespie",
   "url": "https://neilgillespie4senate.blogspot.com/",
   "kind": "campaign_home",
   "title": "Neil J. Gillespie for U.S. Senate",
   "text": "\" John Keker : We don't have to agree on politics but we do have to agree that the legal profession has to protect the rule of law in the United States. Which means lawyers and judges need to be independent from the executive branch. [Yes; see Ex parte Garland, 71 U.S. 333 (1866) ]\""
